bcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=952728#post952728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fullness of time, you will die. That's okay, though. Everyone does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't you turn into Doctor Manhattan and bugger of to your own planet somewhere?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:23:58-07:00","id":953109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=953029#post953029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you turn into Doctor Manhattan and bugger of to your own planet somewhere?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that game's called mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:12:53-07:00","id":953120,"title":"","content":"Not really Mage, no. Not unless you add the whole &quot;and that other planet was the DC universe! And he caused the new 52!&quot; thing from Rebirth. DrM as an Exarch.<br /> <br /> Anyways, he's a goodish example of an accidental Loyalty-led Deviant who finally sucumbs to his own isolation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:10:43-07:00","id":953495,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Endgame</b><br /> <br /> I think what some folks are wondering is if there is a scenario or way for the Deviant to get The Company off their back, keep the powers, and avoid blowout indefinitely. Basically to keep the cool stuff and ditch the Drawbacks- Deviant Golconda.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Mutating Further</b><br /> <br /> Words that come to mind include &quot;Collapse&quot;, &quot;Devolve&quot; or &quot;Warping&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:31:14-07:00","id":953505,"title":"","content":"I'm not against a way out of being a deviant. What I'm against is an easy way out, and keeping your powers without any consequences is way too lazy for me. There should always be a price. For example, if you find a cure, you should be able to go back to being human, but I think it should also cripple you somehow. Maybe you can never walk again, or you go blind, or lose some mental faculty, just to name some examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:34:29-07:00","id":953509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=953495#post953495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Mutating Further</b><br /> <br /> Words that come to mind include &quot;Collapse&quot;, &quot;Devolve&quot; or &quot;Warping&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For a in-universe slang term, &quot;Cronenberging&quot; might work, or at least refering to Deviants twisted but not killed by Blowout as &quot;Cronenbergs&quot; could be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Phrasing 08-18-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:56:55-07:00","id":953601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=953495#post953495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Mutating Further</b><br /> <br /> Words that come to mind include &quot;Collapse&quot;, &quot;Devolve&quot; or &quot;Warping&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Meltdown is another nice one. Both for the nuclear reactor connotations, and because <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SuperPowerMeltdown\" target=\"_blank\">Super Power Meltdown</a> (TVTropes Warning) is already a trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:11:38-07:00","id":953611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=953509#post953509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a in-universe slang term, &amp;quot;Cronenberging&amp;quot; might work, or at least refering to Deviants twisted but not killed by Blowout as &amp;quot;Cronenbergs&amp;quot; could be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would judge this, but Slasher did give us 'Batemans.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T00:22:27-07:00","id":953703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=952484#post952484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only connection to &quot;superhero&quot; media the developers have endorsed are the Marvel Netflix shows, so far Daredevil, and Jessica Jones. Those are plenty gritty. What the Hand want with Elektra is an interesting twist on the pursuing conspiracy angle, the Kingpin models a conspiracy whose goals are orthogonal to the Deviant they come across, and Jessica Jones models an inter-Deviant story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luke Cage next month is looking set to dip right into the Deviant pool with the flashbacks to his origin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:42:06-07:00","id":953745,"title":"","content":"So a couple of questions about Scars...<br /> <br /> 1. How tied are they to Variations? Does each Variation pair to a specific Scar, one of a specific subset of Scars, or potentially with any Scar?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Scars broken down by Origin and Clade?<br /> <br /> 3. Are they necessarily physical, or can you have a psychological issue as your Scar?<br /> <br /> <br /> And another question I'm going spoiler block, because asking it is a spoiler for Sense8:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Is it possible for Deviants to occur more or less naturally?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 08-19-2016, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:27:40-07:00","id":953881,"title":"","content":"One could interpret Alessa from Silent Hill as a Deviant. You even see her blowout in the game's good ending (being pregnant with a god is one hell of a Scar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:16:20-07:00","id":953984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=953881#post953881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could interpret Alessa from Silent Hill as a Deviant. You even see her blowout in the game's good ending (being pregnant with a god is one hell of a Scar).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really would rather see her as Beast - she entwines whole town in her Lair when she get Homecoming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:33:48-07:00","id":954092,"title":"","content":"One idea that, while certain to be untrue, might make a good in-universe theory for certain backgrounds (or maybe a origin for a Promethean game) is that the creation of a Deviant is facilitated by Flux the same way The Created are made when obsession calls down Pyros, regardless of their supposed origins. This, a theorist might claim, is why all Deviants are prone to mutation, degeneration and Blowout; the corupting, entropic Fire within them simply allows no other path, burning Scars into them as its nature dictates. Again, certainly not a Deviant canon, but it might work as the ramblings of an Alchemist or the actual truth in a P:tC-centric game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T18:43:49-07:00","id":954142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=954092#post954092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea that, while certain to be untrue, might make a good in-universe theory for certain backgrounds (or maybe a origin for a Promethean game) is that the creation of a Deviant is facilitated by Flux the same way The Created are made when obsession calls down Pyros, regardless of their supposed origins. This, a theorist might claim, is why all Deviants are prone to mutation, degeneration and Blowout; the corupting, entropic Fire within them simply allows no other path, burning Scars into them as its nature dictates. Again, certainly not a Deviant canon, but it might work as the ramblings of an Alchemist or the actual truth in a P:tC-centric game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could certainly see that being true for alchemical Deviants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T21:52:17-07:00","id":954201,"title":"","content":"I think one of the things I'm going to love the most about Deviant, beyond its Organization rules, will be just how <i>modular </i>it is. You really could do just about any origin you could think of with them, so long as you can work the concept. Translating Deviants into the context of other gamelines is probably going to be one of the first things that I do.<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter for it really can't come soon enough. Can't wait to get a look at the drafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T04:44:48-07:00","id":954304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=954201#post954201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the things I'm going to love the most about Deviant, beyond its Organization rules, will be just how <i>modular </i>it is. You really could do just about any origin you could think of with them, so long as you can work the concept. Translating Deviants into the context of other gamelines is probably going to be one of the first things that I do.<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter for it really can't come soon enough. Can't wait to get a look at the drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what scares me the most and fills me with glee at the same time. The concept is so broad that you can create almost any type of story like mage, but I'm aslo afraid that it may try to include too much and the concept may become diluted. I will trust the developers now, and wait for the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:23:26-07:00","id":954802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=954304#post954304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept is so broad that you can create almost any type of story like mage, but I'm aslo afraid that it may try to include too much and the concept may become diluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was one of the things that led to me trying out changeling, where you could basically play a vampire through the Leechfinger kith, a werewolf through Beasts, and so forth. I think OP's managing to keep up with the evolution in games where people, it seems to me, want more freedom of choice when it comes to creating a character. Even Promethean has added the Extempore without diluting the concept of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T05:27:40-07:00","id":954911,"title":"","content":"A question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> <br /> <br /> Is there going to be a Variation for a mentor? I'm thinking of Conspiracies who're trying to create a new prophet for their god, I quite like the idea of playing that charachter with the god whispering advice in their ear - especially if it has a sinister agenda distinct from the Conspiracy that worships it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:32:27-07:00","id":955180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=954911#post954911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question for <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> Is there going to be a Variation for a mentor? I'm thinking of Conspiracies who're trying to create a new prophet for their god, I quite like the idea of playing that charachter with the god whispering advice in their ear - especially if it has a sinister agenda distinct from the Conspiracy that worships it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd call that &quot;patron&quot; or &quot;symbiont&quot; instead of mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:59:15-07:00","id":955210,"title":"","content":"Rose is a rose is a rose <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:21:53-07:00","id":955669,"title":"","content":"Has there been any information on the source of the Deviant's power? I am wondering if it is a singular source, multiple sources, or &quot;it just happens&quot;?<br /> <br /> I am hoping that there will be a single source but that various conspiracies have tapped that source in different ways. What I mean is that while Deviant X and Deviant Y both have the same source of their weird powers, X was created through technological means while Y was the product of a magical ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:34:27-07:00","id":955678,"title":"","content":"What we've heard implies multiple sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:36:40-07:00","id":955745,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think Deviants are more a &quot;phenomenon&quot; in where all afflicted follow similar rules rather than a specific &quot;kind&quot;, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T05:13:38-07:00","id":956269,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly hoping that's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:28:00-07:00","id":956520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=955669#post955669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any information on the source of the Deviant's power? I am wondering if it is a singular source, multiple sources, or &quot;it just happens&quot;?<br /> <br /> I am hoping that there will be a single source but that various conspiracies have tapped that source in different ways. What I mean is that while Deviant X and Deviant Y both have the same source of their weird powers, X was created through technological means while Y was the product of a magical ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really don't see how a singular source can be behind genetic engineering, cybernetic enhancement, magical superpowers, psychic powers, and things even weirder.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong of course, but I'm thinking that the singular source is &quot;these are all things you can turn a human into.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:06:54-07:00","id":956576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=956520#post956520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't see how a singular source can be behind genetic engineering, cybernetic enhancement, magical superpowers, psychic powers, and things even weirder.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong of course, but I'm thinking that the singular source is &quot;these are all things you can turn a human into.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Deviant is going to be much closer to Promethean than, say, Werewolf in what about their nature unifies characters: Werewolves are variations on a theme who stem from a single source (i.e., descent from Father Wolf and Luna), Prometheans are created through different processes that produce similar results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:04:17-07:00","id":956804,"title":"","content":"Less unified than Promethean, where everything is tied into Alchemy; more like Hunter, I suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:32:05-07:00","id":956872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=956520#post956520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see how a singular source can be behind genetic engineering, cybernetic enhancement, magical superpowers, psychic powers, and things even weirder.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong of course, but I'm thinking that the singular source is &quot;these are all things you can turn a human into.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave's talked about Deviants having their &quot;souls cracked open&quot; - <i>that</i> could easily be a singular phenomenon, even if there are many different things that can make it happen, or alternatively put, many different things that can provoke the trauma causing the subject to react in that way. Then again, if that is a singular phenomenon, it may only be reflected in the power stat, and we know that not all Deviants have one of those (and by impliction, we know that Variations and Scars are largely decoupled from it).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:53:01-07:00","id":956999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=956872#post956872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave's talked about Deviants having their &quot;souls cracked open&quot; - <i>that</i> could easily be a singular phenomenon, even if there are many different things that can make it happen, or alternatively put, many different things that can provoke the trauma causing the subject to react in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default72ce-4.html?g=posts&amp;m=1482843#post1482843\" target=\"_blank\">said a thing on the old forums</a> that feels relevant here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cut my finger last night while I was making chili. I might have done it on a sharp can lid. I might have done it while I was chopping onions with a knife. I could even have taken out my razor and done it on purpose, were I so inclined. But the result is a quarter inch slit in my finger. No matter how I did it, same blood, same risk of infection.<br /> <br /> Vampirism is a wound. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:57:00-07:00","id":957580,"title":"","content":"Question for the mods, when does a project get it's own forum subhead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:01:17-07:00","id":957585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=957580#post957580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the mods, when does a project get it's own forum subhead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Beast didn't get one until it was already out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:19:35-07:00","id":957604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=956999#post956999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default72ce-4.html?g=posts&amp;m=1482843#post1482843&amp;quot;]said</a> a thing on the old forums[/URL] that feels relevant here:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Like vampires, Deviant's game systems describe many different phenomena that are similar enough to share rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:36:44-07:00","id":962128,"title":"","content":"Hm, is Deviant going to be out in time for Dark Eras 2 to have something for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:43:59-07:00","id":962132,"title":"","content":"Beast wasn't out in time for Dark Eras but there was still a stretch goal for a Beast Era, so I'm sure something similar will happen for Deviant, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:12:48-07:00","id":962635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962128#post962128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, is Deviant going to be out in time for Dark Eras 2 to have something for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>it'll be quite hard find a era for deviant. it's a game about human experimentation,and the perios of time where human exoperimentation was a thing were maybe too horrific to put in the book. it'll take a lot of careful decision to pick a era for this game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:27:46-07:00","id":962640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962635#post962635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it'll be quite hard find a era for deviant. it's a game about human experimentation,and the perios of time where human exoperimentation was a thing were maybe too horrific to put in the book. it'll take a lot of careful decision to pick a era for this game</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviants can be magical, too. Ancient Greece gives us Arachne, Medusa, and other people transformed into monsters, who all make ready Deviant fodder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:58:27-07:00","id":962714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962640#post962640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deviants can be magical, too. Ancient Greece gives us Arachne, Medusa, and other people transformed into monsters, who all make ready Deviant fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once DE2 gets rolling, I'm going to be lobbying with you for Deviant/Beast Ancient Greece.<br /> <br /> And you don't have to go Godwin if you want a mad science-themed era- I proposed either the first half the twentieth century (the heyday of pulp scifi) or the middle of it (the Silver Age of Comics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:23:12-07:00","id":962849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962128#post962128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, is Deviant going to be out in time for Dark Eras 2 to have something for it?</div> </div> </div> </div> They should hold out on Dark Eras 2 until Changeling, Giest, Hunter, and Deviant are out. I'd say Mummy as well, but I don't think they'll do a full 2e redo for Mummy, its too rescent, but they might offer up conversion suggestions in the Crossover Chronicle book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:43:09-07:00","id":962854,"title":"","content":"The Victorian era and mid-20th century America might be good Deviant Dark Eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:48:04-07:00","id":962922,"title":"","content":"By the time they get through <b>Changeling</b>, <b>Hunter </b>(not in first drafts), and <b>Geist </b>I'm sure it'll be <b>Mummy</b>'s turn. It would've been up for 2017 anyway, <i>even if</i> all the 2e updates had gone according to schedule of two per year which it hasn't been.<br /> <br /> Even that would've been a five year period between editions, which I think is alright under the <b>CofD</b> circumstances here. I think there's a fair argument people would make that they weren't interested in the game <i>because</i> it wasn't released in 2e. The gameline being recent is why I think OP might not be impatient to get it updated, but I don't think it's reason for us to <i>never</i> see it; that's crazy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:57:01-07:00","id":963058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962635#post962635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it'll be quite hard find a era for deviant. it's a game about human experimentation,and the perios of time where human exoperimentation was a thing were maybe too horrific to put in the book. it'll take a lot of careful decision to pick a era for this game</div> </div> </div> </div> Scientific experimentation doesn't need to be all cronenburg surgery and the like, chemical works as an origin just as well.<br /> <br /> Which is why I suggested the Sixties, the age of &quot;expanding your mind&quot; with drugs was all the rage, in cofd, I'm sure some of those hippies or chemists succeeded in turning on, tuning in, and tuning out of the human race. <br /> <br /> Perhaps in Ancient China someone actually succeeded in chemically induced immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:04:36-07:00","id":963062,"title":"","content":"I just realized Deviant is the <i>perfect</i> game for me to play an old favorite character of mine in.<br /> <br /> YAY!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:49:19-07:00","id":963093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=963058#post963058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I suggested the Sixties, the age of &quot;expanding your mind&quot; with drugs was all the rage, in cofd, I'm sure some of those hippies or chemists succeeded in turning on, tuning in, and tuning out of the human race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a sign that I need to stop neglecting <i>All Along The Watchtowers.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T22:21:31-07:00","id":963105,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping that you can have some sort of Guyver-style symbiont armor. That's one of my all time favorite superpower types. Plus, it's visually distinct and easily lends itself to horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T05:13:08-07:00","id":963171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=962640#post962640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants can be magical, too. Ancient Greece gives us Arachne, Medusa, and other people transformed into monsters, who all make ready Deviant fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Lost Light was coming up with Lucifuge analogies for different conceptions of demon, one of them was sacrifices to Moloch who survived and fought back against the priesthood - and their patron in the case of the hunters. But while I loved it as a hunter concept, I also think it would make an excellent dark era for deviant, since the priesthood will be human - and likely an authority in the setting,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T18:42:47-07:00","id":963478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=963058#post963058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scientific experimentation doesn't need to be all cronenburg surgery and the like, chemical works as an origin just as well.<br /> <br /> Which is why I suggested the Sixties, the age of &quot;expanding your mind&quot; with drugs was all the rage, in cofd, I'm sure some of those hippies or chemists succeeded in turning on, tuning in, and tuning out of the human race.<br /> <br /> Perhaps in Ancient China someone actually succeeded in chemically induced immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that Eleven from <i>Stranger Things</i> is a pretty perfect example of a Deviant, and she gained her powers through her mother's participation in government experiments with LSD and other mind-altering chemicals. So yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T19:48:47-07:00","id":963496,"title":"","content":"Sixties/Cold War Deviant would be AWESOME. Men Who Stare At Goats, radioactive mutant monsters, the CIA trying every trick they can think of to get the upper hand over the reds, and, of course, the aforementioned drug culture. It could probably be combined with my Silver Age of Comics idea, since they cover a lot of the same beats (ie, how hippy culture, social upheaval, and the cold war influenced silver age comics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T20:22:06-07:00","id":963502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=963496#post963496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sixties/Cold War Deviant would be AWESOME. Men Who Stare At Goats, radioactive mutant monsters, the CIA trying every trick they can think of to get the upper hand over the reds, and, of course, the aforementioned drug culture. It could probably be combined with my Silver Age of Comics idea, since they cover a lot of the same beats (ie, how hippy culture, social upheaval, and the cold war influenced silver age comics).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got that pretty soundly pegged as Mage/Hunter, but we'll see how I like Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:59:20-07:00","id":969324,"title":"","content":"The Mage immortality thread (ie, the thread where I made a giant ass of myself) gave me an interesting idea: a mad scientist who turned herself into a lobster-human hybrid seeking immortality. I've wanted to play a werelobster in ChroD for years (do not judge me, we all have dreams), and Deviant looks like the perfect avenue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:04:34-07:00","id":969327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=969324#post969324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage immortality thread (ie, the thread where I made a giant ass of myself) gave me an interesting idea: a mad scientist who turned herself into a lobster-human hybrid seeking immortality. I've wanted to play a werelobster in ChroD for years (do not judge me, we all have dreams), and Deviant looks like the perfect avenue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have many questions but I honestly don't know if I want answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:23:48-07:00","id":969373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=969324#post969324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage immortality thread (ie, the thread where I made a giant ass of myself) gave me an interesting idea: a mad scientist who turned herself into a lobster-human hybrid seeking immortality. I've wanted to play a werelobster in ChroD for years (do not judge me, we all have dreams), and Deviant looks like the perfect avenue.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Zoidberg?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:45:23-07:00","id":969391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=969373#post969373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... Zoidberg?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gritty personal horror biopunk Dr. Zoidberg. The best kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:49:47-07:00","id":969396,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.craveonline.com/images/stories/2011/2012/February/Comedy/zoidberg/zoidberg-header.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> He's a perfect Deviant... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:47:37-07:00","id":972263,"title":"","content":"So, we have confirmation from Dave that there will be a sourcebook released after the core that has information on loyalist Deviants, including how to play them. What other supplements do you think we could see? I'm really hoping for a Night Horrors book, because there are so many possibilities for Deviants that an entire book full of sample characters would work pretty well. Maybe devote the last third of the NH book to some new conspiracies.<br /> <br /> This'll be out in time for Dark Eras 2 and The Crossover Chronicle, right? I feel like there's gonna be a lot of interesting stuff to do with it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:57:37-07:00","id":972555,"title":"","content":"I don't know that there are any supplements I'd be fussed about. It seems like it would be complete as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:02:26-07:00","id":972579,"title":"","content":"I'm keeping sourcebook ideas close to my chest (other than the game's Guide to the Technocracy / Book of the Deceived / etc equivalent) because I will have to talk to Rich at some point about which ones are stretch goals and which we're gonna do regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:51:17-07:00","id":972746,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's totally fair. I mean, the fact that we're getting a guide to playing the antagonist splat at all is fantastic. So far all the news we've gotten about it has made me even more excited. Dave's descriptions of the mechanics look pretty great too. <br /> <br /> I guess I'm mostly asking about other books because Deviant excites me so much and comes from one of my favorite subgenres of horror, so I'm hoping OP does a lot with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:31:28-07:00","id":973035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=972263#post972263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we have confirmation from Dave that there will be a sourcebook released after the core that has information on loyalist Deviants, including how to play them. What other supplements do you think we could see? I'm really hoping for a Night Horrors book, because there are so many possibilities for Deviants that an entire book full of sample characters would work pretty well. Maybe devote the last third of the NH book to some new conspiracies.<br /> <br /> This'll be out in time for Dark Eras 2 and The Crossover Chronicle, right? I feel like there's gonna be a lot of interesting stuff to do with it there.</div> </div> </div> </div> With the book not even out it's a little hard to say what books are really needed.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are the standbys.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a dark era and Mortal remains chapter as stretch goals.<br /> <br /> A storytellers guide for rules and setting hacks is always good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:42:55-07:00","id":973100,"title":"","content":"If FSN isn't an inspiration for Deviant then I will fight you Dave(jk)<br /> <br /> But really I do think that Shirou Emiya is a good exploration on someone broken that is held up by only by an ideal he obsessively pursues, though it lacks the Revenge angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11724,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","user":"backtoback","date":". 09-20-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:43:34-07:00","id":973620,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we'll get options for Deviants that directly use the supernatural power sources of other beings. For example, I have an alchemist character who believes that Prometheans are the next step in human evolution and wishes to become one, and I'm not sure whether to make her as a Promethean or a Pyros-powered Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T03:47:46-07:00","id":973746,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> could I make a really small request?<br /> <br /> Somewehre in the Deviant book, please could you slip in a sidebar with rules for bicycles for that Stranger Things vibe. Or if not rules a quick stat block for use with the existing vehicle rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:24:24-07:00","id":973767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973620#post973620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if we'll get options for Deviants that directly use the supernatural power sources of other beings. For example, I have an alchemist character who believes that Prometheans are the next step in human evolution and wishes to become one, and I'm not sure whether to make her as a Promethean or a Pyros-powered Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the Remade's whole deal is that they're the result of transformation without a guiding &quot;thing&quot; behind it - ghouls, proximi, faetouched, and anything else related to a supernatural being that has a template aren't Deviants.<br /> <br /> The game will be as crossover agnostic as anything that isn't Beast. But you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know: it's the metaphysical line in the sand I've scratched out to stop Deviant consuming all minor templates, which I am actively disinterested in it doing.<br /> <br /> I get that with a new game everyone's first instinct is to think up crossovers and how it affects their ongoing chronicles or favourite, but I'm the guy who won't mention the God-Machine in Mage. Save it for the Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:01:21-07:00","id":973785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973767#post973767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game will be as crossover agnostic as anything that isn't Beast. But you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know: it's the metaphysical line in the sand I've scratched out to stop Deviant consuming all minor templates, which I am actively disinterested in it doing.<br /> <br /> I get that with a new game everyone's first instinct is to think up crossovers and how it affects their ongoing chronicles or favourite, but I'm the guy who won't mention the God-Machine in Mage. Save it for the Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I'd had <i>some</i> hope that it might not be the case, but I'm not surprised or disappointed that it won't be. Though since you bring up the Crossover Chronicle, deviants with enough connection to the forces behind other lines to use their fuel - and a vitae-fuelled deviant is still not much like a ghoul - seems like a valid subject for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:25:38-07:00","id":973803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973767#post973767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game will be as crossover agnostic as anything that isn't Beast. But you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know: it's the metaphysical line in the sand I've scratched out to stop Deviant consuming all minor templates, which I am actively disinterested in it doing.<br /> <br /> I get that with a new game everyone's first instinct is to think up crossovers and how it affects their ongoing chronicles or favourite, but I'm the guy who won't mention the God-Machine in Mage. Save it for the Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the crossover chronicles include Merits or Variations that allow a Deviant to be fueled by existing power stats?<br /> <br /> I approve of your crossover agnostic direction, I certainly wouldn't want Deviants consuming other minor templates, but personally I see a clear distinction between Deviants and, e.g. Proximus. Cheifly a Deviant's need for an external axis of identity and the risk of their powers going critical.<br /> <br /> So basically. I don't see the risks of Deviant consuming minor tempaltes. But I quite like the idea of a Deviant created by a Mage's botched attempt to force an Awakening being able to use Mana.<br /> <hr />Actually now I think about it I'm curious.<br /> <br /> Do all Deviants share a power source, or do you choose a power source and methods of refueling as part of creating a charachter? It's an extremely broad splat so I could easily see the cyborg needing to steal or buy replacement fuel rods on the black market while the psychic is using plain old Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-21-2016, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:40:41-07:00","id":973814,"title":"","content":"Who says they have a fuel stat at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:52:38-07:00","id":973826,"title":"","content":"I'm taking it that they don't. That both makes sense and makes them more unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:55:28-07:00","id":973827,"title":"","content":"The option I'm hoping to see is that you can use your powers and abilities whenever you want, without fuel, but the penalty is that you open your scar, or scars, and can even make them worse. Power at the expense of your health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:35:17-07:00","id":973843,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how most Deviants view and relate to the &quot;lesser&quot; splats created or related to the major supernatural powers, such as ghouls, proximi, wolf-blooded, etc. <br /> <br /> Although as Dave often mentions, broad generalizations should be avoided, I'm curious if the prevailing view sees these lesser supernatural templates that, for the most part, have good relations with their &quot;parent&quot; splats with envy and jealousy, disgust, or if they're just too busy running to give it much consideration.<br /> <br /> Also, as a setting matter, do Deviants seek out other major supernaturals like mages to find cures or sanctuary? <br /> <br /> I hope these issues mentioned in Deviant and directly addressed in the Crossover Chronicles,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:36:13-07:00","id":973898,"title":"","content":"A question: how &quot;Read In&quot; heavy is deviant ? I mean how much does a player need to read to enjoy playing the game. More on the heavy part (like Werewolf/Mage - those have a ton of setting material that PC are somewhat assumed to know and there's a lot of mechanics) or the less heavy (Hunter, where it's possible to play on the &quot;there are monsters and you hunt them&quot; lvl).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:42:23-07:00","id":973901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973814#post973814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says they have a fuel stat at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>My current assumption is that they do if they have dots in their power stat, and don't otherwise. Unless there's a particular Variation that grants it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:49:27-07:00","id":973954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973898#post973898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question: how &quot;Read In&quot; heavy is deviant ? I mean how much does a player need to read to enjoy playing the game. More on the heavy part (like Werewolf/Mage - those have a ton of setting material that PC are somewhat assumed to know and there's a lot of mechanics) or the less heavy (Hunter, where it's possible to play on the &quot;there are monsters and you hunt them&quot; lvl).</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've read so far and from the basic concept of the game, I'd say it's probably more of the latter. Think of shows like Stranger Things or movies like Firestarter. The &quot;experiment&quot; doesn't necessarily know much about the organization that created them. They may not know much about the world at all. Trying to find out who is trying to hunt you down is usually part of the challenge of keeping your freedom (or exacting your revenge). So I'd say the players could go into the game almost blind to anything beyond the basic elements needed to play that specific character. <br /> <br /> &quot;All you know is the Farm. The Farm raised you. You never knew there was anything other than the Farm. And then they made you kill the kitten, and something broke inside you. You don't remember how you escaped. You don't know where you are. You don't know why they're hunting you. All you know is that you have to run... and that you can kill with your mind.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:29:17-07:00","id":974001,"title":"","content":"I think aside from having a hand in creating the group hunting you character, its not going to be as setting/knowledge intensive as say Mage/Werewolf/Geist/Changeling.<br /> <br /> If I had to make a guess from what we've heard so far, I'd say it'll be more like Hunter/Vampire/Promeathan instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:43:31-07:00","id":974040,"title":"","content":"Is there any setting to know in Deviant? I thought you built your own opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:25:57-07:00","id":974098,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the information we're getting from this Dave Brookshaw fella. If memory serves he was the main guy behind Mage 2E, heavily involved in Mummy and a multitude of other works. Sticking him in charge do Deviant too, the work load would be too much for any normal guy. (Or in other words, jeez Dave, I appreciate the work you do for us hungry gamers, hope you don't get too burned out on it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:25:47-07:00","id":974129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974040#post974040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any setting to know in Deviant? I thought you built your own opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they will give us a couple of examples to use as opposition and then give us rules to create our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:04:31-07:00","id":974341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974129#post974129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they will give us a couple of examples to use as opposition and then give us rules to create our own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been said, yeah - there's talk of the Cheiron group being one of the examples, but that depends on Monica Valentinelli signing off on it. My certainly that the Hototogisu will be one of them knows no bounds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: the Variations can be balanced by Scars or points for the ST to build opposition. Is the default intent going to be that the campaign has the same organisation hunting all the PC's or different ones, or no default on that score? (One group adds more focus, and with the points from the whole group can be more powerful - but makes it less likely that it would have created very different sorts of deviant - and also less likely, though by a smaller margin, that it would think deviants outside its usual focus are things it can make use of).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:17:01-07:00","id":974343,"title":"","content":"Hototogisu will likely be in Deviants Tokyo section at the very least. Heck I think Hototogisu is mentioned in most of the game lines Tokyo section, its got its fingers in a lot of pies.<br /> <br /> And Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-22-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:31:49-07:00","id":974506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974341#post974341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's been said, yeah - there's talk of the Cheiron group being one of the examples, but that depends on Monica Valentinelli signing off on it. My certainly that the Hototogisu will be one of them knows no bounds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: the Variations can be balanced by Scars or points for the ST to build opposition. Is the default intent going to be that the campaign has the same organisation hunting all the PC's or different ones, or no default on that score? (One group adds more focus, and with the points from the whole group can be more powerful - but makes it less likely that it would have created very different sorts of deviant - and also less likely, though by a smaller margin, that it would think deviants outside its usual focus are things it can make use of).</div> </div> </div> </div>One group, although practical, will not be realistic taking into account the different trypes of deviants. I was thinking more in the lines of giving us five examples of classic archetypes of evil organizations since it seems that the developers are obsessed with the number five, here are some examples:<br /> <br /> - A secret government branch responsible for creating super soldier cyborgs.<br /> - A think tank of scientists seeking to unlock the powers of the human mind with drugs.<br /> - A cult that's perfecting a ritual to create a door to their god through human sacrifice.<br /> - A corporation that creates mutant animal hybrids to sell to the highest bidder.<br /> - A ancient order that uses alchemy to transform their members into something inhuman.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:00:43-07:00","id":974648,"title":"","content":"So, it feels to me like Deviant is kind of the anti-Beast, and that's real neat. I like Beast, mind, but it's still neat to see a game that pulls out basically the opposite of its themes, and I'm interested to see some Beast/Deviant interactions. Especially if I can play a Deviant with a Horror forcefully bonded to him as an origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:55:49-07:00","id":974748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973767#post973767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the Remade's whole deal is that they're the result of transformation without a guiding &amp;quot;thing&amp;quot; behind it - ghouls, proximi, faetouched, and anything else related to a supernatural being that has a template aren't Deviants.<br /> <br /> The game will be as crossover agnostic as anything that isn't Beast. But you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know: it's the metaphysical line in the sand I've scratched out to stop Deviant consuming all minor templates, which I am actively disinterested in it doing.<br /> <br /> I get that with a new game everyone's first instinct is to think up crossovers and how it affects their ongoing chronicles or favourite, but I'm the guy who won't mention the God-Machine in Mage. Save it for the Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm a crossover nut but I can totally understand this from a gameplay and writing standpoint. Was hoping we'd get some sample conspiracies based on different lines, but like you've said, that's something that the fandom is doing a lot of on its own. <br /> <br /> Hoping TCC will have some options for that, but I don't think it'll be that hard to work out some crossover characters. Still, this is making me wonder if I should do that alchemist as a Promethean character instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:31:46-07:00","id":974772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974648#post974648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it feels to me like Deviant is kind of the anti-Beast, and that's real neat. I like Beast, mind, but it's still neat to see a game that pulls out basically the opposite of its themes, and I'm interested to see some Beast/Deviant interactions. Especially if I can play a Deviant with a Horror forcefully bonded to him as an origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I want a Beast/Deviant crossover romping around Mythic Greece for exactly this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:33:07-07:00","id":974773,"title":"","content":"Low-powered, obviously supernatural protagonists with special Traits revolving around how they bond with or hate other people?<br /> <br /> Yeah, come to think of it, it <i>is</i> a contrast to Beast. Deviant's got piles upon piles of modern-day inspirational media, too, but struggles with historical settings, while Beast's all over traditional monster legends but theres fewer tv shows you can watch and think &quot;that's Beast&quot;.<br /> <br /> Doing the same game over and over again would be <i>boring</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:47:55-07:00","id":974806,"title":"","content":"Deviant getting a Mortal Remains supplement like Beast would be neat, though tough to imagine what a Deviant oriented hunter group that doesn't just feel like an organization trying to retrieve one of the loose renegades would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:51:35-07:00","id":974807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974806#post974806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant getting a Mortal Remains supplement like Beast would be neat, though tough to imagine what a Deviant oriented hunter group that doesn't just feel like an organization trying to retrieve one of the loose renegades would be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be a group that is like Cheiron except they get all their research through &quot;industrial espionage&quot;, they don't know how to make deviants so they try to learn secrets of occult sciences by sending out their hunters to attack and kidnapping the deviants of other corporations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:07:18-07:00","id":974817,"title":"","content":"Yeah I suppose if it's along the lines of 3rd party corporate sabotage and espionage it could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:24:21-07:00","id":974844,"title":"","content":"Or they're some group that wants to cure them, and damned if their total ignorance of the situation is going to stop them from trying!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:26:47-07:00","id":975024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974506#post974506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One group, although practical, will not be realistic taking into account the different trypes of deviants. I was thinking more in the lines of giving us five examples of classic archetypes of evil organizations since it seems that the developers are obsessed with the number five, here are some examples:<br /> <br /> - A secret government branch responsible for creating super soldier cyborgs.<br /> - A think tank of scientists seeking to unlock the powers of the human mind with drugs.<br /> - A cult that's perfecting a ritual to create a door to their god through human sacrifice.<br /> - A corporation that creates mutant animal hybrids to sell to the highest bidder.<br /> - A ancient order that uses alchemy to transform their members into something inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood me. I meant the default intent over whether <i>a given campaign</i> would use one organisation or more.<br /> <br /> I like your examples, thoiugh.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:12:16-07:00","id":975249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975024#post975024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you misunderstood me. I meant the default intent over whether <i>a given campaign</i> would use one organisation or more.<br /> <br /> I like your examples, thoiugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any way in which the group sharing a conspiracy works as the default assumption of the game (someone's particular campaign sure, as the game default it would either mean the game makes no sense or the players are handicapped from making the characters they want), and that's before it was revealed that one of the results of a deviant increasing their powers is that the organization hunting them becomes more formidable in balance.<br /> <br /> Which would mean that if one or two players decided to develop their powers while everyone else developed skills and merits that the latter would be screwed over by the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:25:25-07:00","id":975296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=974773#post974773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low-powered, obviously supernatural protagonists with special Traits revolving around how they bond with or hate other people?<br /> <br /> Yeah, come to think of it, it <i>is</i> a contrast to Beast. Deviant's got piles upon piles of modern-day inspirational media, too, but struggles with historical settings, while Beast's all over traditional monster legends but theres fewer tv shows you can watch and think &amp;quot;that's Beast&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Doing the same game over and over again would be <i>boring</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd go with Saints (Christian, Buddist, Hindu, ect...) as a potential starting point for a historical era, along with the ancient heroes and Monsters from Greece as others have suggested as good starting points for a historical eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:57:42-07:00","id":975568,"title":"","content":"I miss z-splats.<br /> <br /> Are we ever going to see them again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:24:28-07:00","id":975576,"title":"","content":"When I think about historical periods for deviant what I can see is the inter-war and WW2 period a fitting one. Cause nazis and inhuman experiments trying to make super soldiers is a classic.<br /> <br /> Cold war soviet russia could also work. Though the settings could be really grimm.<br /> <br /> 19-20 age could be fun too, as an age where science bloomed and people were making experiments quite frequently disregarding safety. Also it's an age of clash between reason and the belief in supernatural. Like if instead of dieing of radiation poisoning Marie Curie got something far weirder.<br /> <br /> @up: Unless I'm mistake Dave in one of hes APs once said that he loved z-splats. So, possibly, i think :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 09-24-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:39:51-07:00","id":975586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975568#post975568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss z-splats.<br /> <br /> Are we ever going to see them again?</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling will have z splats, but the core will only have a few of them, with more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T12:23:55-07:00","id":975643,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but none of the new lines have had them. I think Beast could have gotten away with it at least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:04:07-07:00","id":975664,"title":"","content":"Hard Core Henry is a VERY gonzo Deviant story, with a built in reason to crossover with werewolf due to the cross over between the movie and Payday 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T19:49:04-07:00","id":975784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975643#post975643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but none of the new lines have had them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last three lines have all been running somewhere in the headspace that other gamelines accord to world-stage movers and shakers with a volume slider bolted on. Z-splats generally assume a structure that's less ad-hoc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:09:23-07:00","id":975815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975643#post975643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but none of the new lines have had them. I think Beast could have gotten away with it at least</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy <i>kinda</i> has them in the form of Movements, but given that those are only for the antagonists...<br /> <br /> ...huh. I wonder if any Arisen Movements exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:22:12-07:00","id":975819,"title":"","content":"so last night I've dreamed that I've had the Deviant rulebook, and that it had a big section about history and such- for example, it tied the origin of Deviant to the Big Bang or something like that :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T00:54:38-07:00","id":975875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975568#post975568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss z-splats.<br /> <br /> Are we ever going to see them again?</div> </div> </div> </div>They take up too much room.<br /> <br /> For reals, it's a practical consideration - Mage had to leave stuff out to get the Legacy rules in, Vampire and Werewolf didn't manage to get bloodlines and lodges. There just isn't enough room in a corebook to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T01:57:09-07:00","id":975885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975875#post975875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They take up too much room.<br /> <br /> For reals, it's a practical consideration - Mage had to leave stuff out to get the Legacy rules in, Vampire and Werewolf didn't manage to get bloodlines and lodges. There just isn't enough room in a corebook to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, besides, not even Hasbro included prestige classes on the first volume of the PC guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:13:08-07:00","id":976065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975875#post975875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They take up too much room.<br /> <br /> For reals, it's a practical consideration - Mage had to leave stuff out to get the Legacy rules in, Vampire and Werewolf didn't manage to get bloodlines and lodges. There just isn't enough room in a corebook to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know if that person was refering to Z splats in the corebooks or just later on.<br /> <br /> If you guys don't want to do Z-splat books anymore, you could just hire someone to write a translation guide for all the old Z-Splats, say a Bloodlines translation guide, no new fluff except were needed, just mostly update the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:55:56-07:00","id":976469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975249#post975249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any way in which the group sharing a conspiracy works as the default assumption of the game (someone's particular campaign sure, as the game default it would either mean the game makes no sense or the players are handicapped from making the characters they want)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, once again, I <i>was</i> talking about individual campaigns. If every PC is being hunted by a different group, that could make campaigns very scrambled - and we already know that some of the GM'ing advice will be dealing with character mortality and replacement, which would only exacerbate such scrambling. On the other hand, a single given group is unlikely to be making the whole range of possible PC's - it might be interested in capturing or killing a wider range than that, though - but it still puts more focus on any PC's who <i>were</i> made by it. So I wonder if the default-assumed campaign will be a limited range of PC types with single or few adversaries, or wide range of PC types with individual adversaries - or if it will attempt not to make a default assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975875#post975875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They take up too much room.<br /> <br /> For reals, it's a practical consideration - Mage had to leave stuff out to get the Legacy rules in, Vampire and Werewolf didn't manage to get bloodlines and lodges. There just isn't enough room in a corebook to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might they appear in supplements, or are they gone for good?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:13:45-07:00","id":976488,"title":"","content":"Well, the newer games (including, as it happens, Deviant) are designed without them, so stapling them on would be odd. Or something for a player's guide.<br /> <br /> But in Deviant's case, no. You have to build a Conspiracy for your character to oppose, and that's taking up the mechanical space in both pagecount and asked-for effort on the part of a troupe that a z-splat would take. Same deal as Mummy Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:55:23-07:00","id":976501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976488#post976488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in Deviant's case, no. You have to build a Conspiracy for your character to oppose, and that's taking up the mechanical space in both pagecount and asked-for effort on the part of a troupe that a z-splat would take. Same deal as Mummy Cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, as far as Z-splats goes. But do I take this to imply that a character's opposing conspiracy is player- rather than GM-designed?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:00:36-07:00","id":976592,"title":"","content":"Since we're talking splats,i've been thinking about Clades,givent the source material. could something like possesion from a entity from another dimension be a Clade?Maybe someone who had some organs trade by demonic organs? Could there be a Clade based on captain america style super-soldiers? or is that something all deviants can be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:38:07-07:00","id":976607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976469#post976469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, once again, I <i>was</i> talking about individual campaigns. If every PC is being hunted by a different group, that could make campaigns very scrambled - and we already know that some of the GM'ing advice will be dealing with character mortality and replacement, which would only exacerbate such scrambling. On the other hand, a single given group is unlikely to be making the whole range of possible PC's - it might be interested in capturing or killing a wider range than that, though - but it still puts more focus on any PC's who <i>were</i> made by it. So I wonder if the default-assumed campaign will be a limited range of PC types with single or few adversaries, or wide range of PC types with individual adversaries - or if it will attempt not to make a default assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm really curious to see how they handle this, but I trust the team to find a clean way to make it work. I see two potential ways to make this work.<br /> <br /> One way would be to make conspiracies BIG. Say, you have an arm of American or Russian intelligence that breaks their superhuman research into a bunch of sub-departments and all uses an elite wing of the military to track down escaped subjects. Or you have something like the Cheiron Corporation that specializes in splicing together a wide variety of monster parts onto their experiments.<br /> <br /> The other alternative I see is to have these conspiracies using contractors. Say most of them are research groups that don't have their own military/security arm, so they tend to utilize mercenary groups and bounty hunters that specialize in hunting deviants. Stack on opportunists and branches of the military that are focused on containment and neutralization of all mad science gone amok, and you have unified threats for the players to band against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:06:40-07:00","id":976808,"title":"","content":"I kinda think of it like Night's Black Agents conspiracy pyramids: maybe the conspiracies of individual Renegades are a mid to high rung on the ladder, and an even grander conspiracy is secretly manipulating <i>them</i>. So the PCs are going about their everyday business of fighting their tailored enemies only to unravel the truth that even those are just pawns of something more sinister","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:15:13-07:00","id":976882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976808#post976808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think of it like Night's Black Agents conspiracy pyramids: maybe the conspiracies of individual Renegades are a mid to high rung on the ladder, and an even grander conspiracy is secretly manipulating <i>them</i>. So the PCs are going about their everyday business of fighting their tailored enemies only to unravel the truth that even those are just pawns of something more sinister</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man behind the Man, or This Isn't Even My Final Form (organization version)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T03:04:12-07:00","id":977085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976808#post976808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think of it like Night's Black Agents conspiracy pyramids: maybe the conspiracies of individual Renegades are a mid to high rung on the ladder, and an even grander conspiracy is secretly manipulating <i>them</i>. So the PCs are going about their everyday business of fighting their tailored enemies only to unravel the truth that even those are just pawns of something more sinister</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O3s1H37KxH4\" data-code=\"O3s1H37KxH4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/O3s1H37KxH4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:51:29-07:00","id":977368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976808#post976808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think of it like Night's Black Agents conspiracy pyramids: maybe the conspiracies of individual Renegades are a mid to high rung on the ladder, and an even grander conspiracy is secretly manipulating <i>them</i>. So the PCs are going about their everyday business of fighting their tailored enemies only to unravel the truth that even those are just pawns of something more sinister</div> </div> </div> </div> Certainly possible, but I was thinking more along the lines of economics.<br /> <br /> If a deviant has minor powers, well, the organization presumably has other stuff to do, so its not going to throw anything other than minor resources for a minor reward.<br /> <br /> But a deviant who hulked out, well the organization is going to be willing to put out nuclear option resources for nuclear level benefits.<br /> <br /> And if a conspiracy doesn't have the appropriate resources? Well then the logical thing is that they'd give up, find some other deviant they have the resources to handle. In which case some other conspiracy will find out about the deviant and start hunting them. <br /> <br /> Maybe if they have friendly contact with another conspiracy they might suggest a group project to stay in the game. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:50:55-07:00","id":977411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=976808#post976808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think of it like Night's Black Agents conspiracy pyramids: maybe the conspiracies of individual Renegades are a mid to high rung on the ladder, and an even grander conspiracy is secretly manipulating <i>them</i>. So the PCs are going about their everyday business of fighting their tailored enemies only to unravel the truth that even those are just pawns of something more sinister</div> </div> </div> </div>If <i>Deviant</i> steals the Conspyramid it'll instantly shoot up in my personal approval. <br /> <br /> Honestly, building the antagonist Conspiracies is the part of this game that I'm most looking forward to, though I'm sure that'll change with some more spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:05:20-07:00","id":977423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=977411#post977411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If <i>Deviant</i> steals the Conspyramid it'll instantly shoot up in my personal approval.<br /> <br /> Honestly, building the antagonist Conspiracies is the part of this game that I'm most looking forward to, though I'm sure that'll change with some more spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. I love the idea of the player group working together to build their own collective antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:16:07-07:00","id":977459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=977411#post977411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If <i>Deviant</i> steals the Conspyramid it'll instantly shoot up in my personal approval.<br /> <br /> Honestly, building the antagonist Conspiracies is the part of this game that I'm most looking forward to, though I'm sure that'll change with some more spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Conspyramid&quot; sounds like a good name for a band.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:14:32-07:00","id":977486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=975784#post975784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last three lines have all been running somewhere in the headspace that other gamelines accord to world-stage movers and shakers with a volume slider bolted on. Z-splats generally assume a structure that's less ad-hoc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I diagree about <b>Beast</b>, though. I don't see them as world-stage, but that could just be me being wrong.<br /> <br /> I still think Z-splats would've done them good, at least, whether it's further customizing the type of Horror they are/represent, giving them more 'typical' social organizations, or further evolving the Kinship they share with other monsters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:43:44-07:00","id":977496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=977486#post977486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I diagree about <b>Beast</b>, though. I don't see them as world-stage, but that could just be me being wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence &quot;with a volume-slider bolted on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thicker Than Water and the Lair are essentially Archmastery As Status and the Golden Road (plus Chantries) adjusted for street-level starting-character viability, particularly taken in combination with Nightmares-as-Social-Maneuvering's overlap with the tendency of other gamelines' god-equivalents to make frequent use of dreams as plan.<br /> <br /> A Beast who hunts the deserts in Nevada can return there with comparative ease for as long as they have a desert Chamber even if they move to Morocco, and they're equipped to find and recruit supernatural agents in short order through direct or indirect means, especially as they grow in power.<br /> <br /> That's at least as world-stage as Mummy's &quot;you start activity at the height of your power and are basically assumed to have a decent-sized cadre of mortal agents at your disposal&quot; or Demon's &quot;your abilities and expertise allow you to exploit the great engine that runs the mortal sphere with varying degrees of power and subtlety even if you aren't burning mortal lives to move mountains in the short term.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:53:37-07:00","id":977710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=977496#post977496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence &quot;with a volume-slider bolted on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:42:41-07:00","id":978010,"title":"","content":"I came up with the idea of a mortal cult of Master Shapers with a Hollow, that are experimenting with using Hedge Warping to try and fuse parts of the Hedge with humans.<br /> <br /> This usually ends in death of the mortal, but sometimes the Hedge ends up embedded in the humans soul, causing to break, turning them into deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:27:29-07:00","id":978029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=978010#post978010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came up with the idea of a mortal cult of Master Shapers with a Hollow, that are experimenting with using Hedge Warping to try and fuse parts of the Hedge with humans.<br /> <br /> This usually ends in death of the mortal, but sometimes the Hedge ends up embedded in the humans soul, causing to break, turning them into deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting concept. So are they physically tied to the Hedge? Or do they have a bit of the Wyrd in place of their soul?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972806-101-deviant-orgs\">Also, I started a thread for Org ideas that you might wanna look at.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:28:43-07:00","id":978216,"title":"","content":"As much as I'd want this book to have a three hundred page section on crossovers and another three hundred pages about sample organizations and z-splats, I can't argue with either of those decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:46:59-07:00","id":978330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=977368#post977368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if a conspiracy doesn't have the appropriate resources? Well then the logical thing is that they'd give up, find some other deviant they have the resources to handle. In which case some other conspiracy will find out about the deviant and start hunting them.<br /> <br /> Maybe if they have friendly contact with another conspiracy they might suggest a group project to stay in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is that a conspiracy that comes across deviant clades outside its direct sphere of expertise may try to hunt down such deviants for study - but if it becomes aware of those who already know about them, may go after <i>that</i> group instead - why research when you can steal another's research? In which case, if the PC's are being hunted by different groups, it opens the tactic of pitting those groups against one another.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:44:35-07:00","id":978541,"title":"","content":"I've been off of the forums for a bit, so this is literally the first time I've heard of this new game...wow, and I'd just gotten the basics of Beast down! Frankly, given how versatile BtP was, possibly the ultimate expression of &quot;You play the Monster&quot; yet, I was getting worried about where WW would go from there, so I'm glad to see there are still new ideas on the way!<br /> <br /> My first thought was that Deviant sounded a bit like Aberrant, esp with the mutations taking over like Taint, but I love the image of interacting with humanity as a way to reign in the Scars. The Developer mentioned Orphan Black as an inspiration, but I can't stop thinking of Gotham, with its flood of &quot;freaks&quot; escaping from the secret Conspiracy underneath Arkham Asylum as a good example. <br /> <br /> It sounds like this is going to have more of a sci-fi bent? Deviants may well have more variants to their splats than even Changeling, but The Lost are all still the same creatures from the same origin. If Deviants are really from so many disparate sources, then how can they reasonably have the same base mechanics? As far as Xovers go, I can see them finding the most in common with Prometheans and Demons, both for being created by &quot;mad science&quot; and for hiding out on the run from their creators.<br /> <br /> Apologies if these were answered elsewhere, I read the beginning and end of this thread, but was too excited to plow thru it all before posting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:37:55-07:00","id":978591,"title":"","content":"Mad science is only one option, though it <i>is</i> one option. Deviants can be magical or alchemical or such like as well.<br /> <br /> The reason why they have the same mechanics is that they're defined not by origin, but effect - their &quot;souls are cracked open&quot; - no, I'm not sure what that means either, but many of the effects will be consistent no matter what prompted it. Satchel posted a quote from Rose Bailey about this: in summary, a wound on your finger might have been caused by a knife, a claw, or paper, and might have been an accident, someone hurting you, you hurting yourself; but the wound is the same, regardless. Changeling's defined by the &quot;someone hurting you,&quot; Deviant's defined by the &quot;it's a wound&quot; (and yes, you can have done it to yourself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:03:09-07:00","id":978723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=978029#post978029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting concept. So are they physically tied to the Hedge? Or do they have a bit of the Wyrd in place of their soul?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972806-101-deviant-orgs\">Also, I started a thread for Org ideas that you might wanna look at.</a></div> </div> </div> </div> More like one or more of the thorns piercing their soul, with their soul nourishing the thorns enough that the piece of Hedge lodged in them don't decay Ironside (earth).<br /> <br /> So they aren't Fae, just fundalmentally changed by the Thorns (piece of Hedge, might not literally be Thorns) piercing their soul.<br /> <br /> It doesn't give them a Wyrd stat, just transforns them spiritually and physically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:59:39-07:00","id":978987,"title":"","content":"If I recall it was mentioned that parasites/symbiotes would be possible for Deviant? (Since there was also mention of stuff like Guyver fitting under the category)<br /> <br /> Been prepping ahead of time for a campaign idea once the book comes out, of the players being employees of a research facility in Antarctica that records and looks at the life in the area, primarily the stuff that is in the deep surrounding ice filled waters. One of the deep sea crews come back with something they found frozen in the ice that they want to document. Later of course the ice containing the specimens breaks and they get loose in the lab and like any good parasite, through their roaming through vents and things find their way to and attach to the party members, before everything starts fading to black and sirens and alarms are flaring. When they eventually wake up they find that the whole facility has been put into lockdown stuck with each other and other employees who either scared of them or want these scary former co-workers dead, as well as possibly other parasites that might be a bit more out of control/less rational. Would be a bit of a game of trying to break out of the facility and escape before the companies containment unit arrives from outside to capture them.<br /> <br /> Would this be possible to run with Deviant? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:52:05-07:00","id":980043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=978591#post978591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mad science is only one option, though it <i>is</i> one option. Deviants can be magical or alchemical or such like as well.<br /> <br /> The reason why they have the same mechanics is that they're defined not by origin, but effect - their &quot;souls are cracked open&quot; - no, I'm not sure what that means either, but many of the effects will be consistent no matter what prompted it. Satchel posted a quote from Rose Bailey about this: in summary, a wound on your finger might have been caused by a knife, a claw, or paper, and might have been an accident, someone hurting you, you hurting yourself; but the wound is the same, regardless. Changeling's defined by the &quot;someone hurting you,&quot; Deviant's defined by the &quot;it's a wound&quot; (and yes, you can have done it to yourself).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I was going off the dev's mention of playing as cyborgs and psychics, but it doesn't take much to imagine oneself mutating into some sort of eldritch abomination. Still, even if they're that diverse, I imagine there's *something*, whether a shared power stat or similar mechanic or the &quot;wound&quot;, that lets them identify each other and congregate. I wonder what their teams and larger groupings (if any) are called?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:34:40-07:00","id":981431,"title":"","content":"Anyone here read Glen Bullion's Damned and Cursed series (if not, you should)? Alex as a reluctant beast and Jack Kursed as a deviant are concepts both of which make me very happy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:10:03-07:00","id":981447,"title":"","content":"Will Deviant have the narrative stretch to cover a story where a group of Minor psychics is experimented on to increase their power and instead forms a gestalt where they are stuck more powerful but also permanently sharing brain space with each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:48:23-07:00","id":981466,"title":"","content":"Is the rather excellent Jekyll (BBC show with James Nesbit) considered as source for Deviant. Elements are there, experiment and backlash against a controlling organization but spaced out since the experiment actually happened to the MCs progenitor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:50:14-07:00","id":983598,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am really excited for Deviant, and having seen some of the spoilers Daveb gave way back, decided to make a few guesses as to what could be in Deviant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Power Fuel-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What with the character possibilities being so diverse, and their \u201cstate\u201d being no guided one, I guess there is *not* a Fuel Stat like we have seen in other games. The closest I think we will get is similar to the \u201cConviction\u201d add-on for Mortals/Hunters in a past shard book (Mirrors, I think). Likely, they will have a higher or seperate Willpower pool, which can (but not always) fuel their powers. A few hints put the \u201ccost\u201d of their Variations being the Scars, it seems. Scars likely can include Willpower cost, but not always. (Ex: Eleven doesn\u2019t spend Willpower to activate her Telekineses, but takes Bashing damage per activation, though she can spend Willpower to augment her Variation).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m guessing this because the Remade and the game feels very Driven, Determined, etc, and Willpower being the extension of that, makes me guess it will become more important to these characters, similar to Hunter (and some extent, Mage and Mummy). The least, they will have more oppurtunities to gain Willpower than the normal Mortal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clade- \u201cHost\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Host is Shinichi Izumi (of Parasyte, anime and manga), a boy whose right arm was consumed and replaced by an \u201calien\u201d parasyte named Migi, one with its own intelligence and instinct, though little personality.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Host is Jackie Estacado, invaded by The Darkness, via patrilineal ritual that connects him with the (very powerful) embodiment of Darkness. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Host has *something* inside them, either physically or otherwise. It has infected them, and has a minor will of its own. Their Variations tend to have Scars where the other Entity takes control of the power for a time, or tries to urge the Host to do things he wouldn\u2019t. These characters never feel alone, and their path is littered with accidents and tragedy caused by something they can\u2019t rid of. In the end, they too often try to take their own lives (which the entity likely does not abide), or die trying to \u201cremove\u201d the entity inside, unable to undo the process that binded them. And that's if they are lucky, and don\u2019t become a hollow shell, their identity and/or flesh subsumed by a hostile entity, as it uses its new Body for its inhuman ends.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2377-wyrm-sage","name":"Wyrm Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T06:02:52-07:00","id":983876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyrm Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=983598#post983598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What with the character possibilities being so diverse, and their \u201cstate\u201d being no guided one, I guess there is *not* a Fuel Stat like we have seen in other games. The closest I think we will get is similar to the \u201cConviction\u201d add-on for Mortals/Hunters in a past shard book (Mirrors, I think). Likely, they will have a higher or seperate Willpower pool, which can (but not always) fuel their powers ... I\u2019m guessing this because the Remade and the game feels very Driven, Determined, etc, and Willpower being the extension of that, makes me guess it will become more important to these characters, similar to Hunter (and some extent, Mage and Mummy). The least, they will have more oppurtunities to gain Willpower than the normal Mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. We know there is a power stat, though not all Deviants have it, and it only goes up to 5. It adds to their supernatural tolerance (= it + their highest level of Variation) - but I assume that's not all it does. I mentioned earlier that my current assumption is that Deviants with the power stat also have a fuel stat, but others don't; I assume this because there isn't much else for a power stat that only goes up to 5 to do. However, the same could also be covered by it granting and covering the extra Willpower options you describe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Host has *something* inside them, either physically or otherwise. It has infected them, and has a minor will of its own. Their Variations tend to have Scars where the other Entity takes control of the power for a time, or tries to urge the Host to do things he wouldn\u2019t. These characters never feel alone, and their path is littered with accidents and tragedy caused by something they can\u2019t rid of. In the end, they too often try to take their own lives (which the entity likely does not abide), or die trying to \u201cremove\u201d the entity inside, unable to undo the process that binded them. And that's if they are lucky, and don\u2019t become a hollow shell, their identity and/or flesh subsumed by a hostile entity, as it uses its new Body for its inhuman ends. </div> </div> </div>I hope you're right about this. (Though I can't stand Jackie Estacado; the Witchblade could be considered in a similar light though).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:39:50-07:00","id":988068,"title":"","content":"So come to think of it, depending on how flexible the powers are, you could probably reproduce all the Splats thus far (except possibly Mages, just because of their sheer breadth of power) with a fair bit of reliability. Obviously, it'd be kept within Deviant power scale, but this could make crossover games a bit more workable (you're playing Deviant, one guy wants to play a Vampire, make him stat it up with Deviant rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:09:36-07:00","id":989444,"title":"","content":"Apologies if anyone has mentioned this but without getting into spoilers, Nightvale Presents' second newest podcast: Within the Wires is sounding a lot like a Deviant prologue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:07:06-07:00","id":989528,"title":"","content":"Hm, you could still work Mages as Deviants- I like the idea that every formerly-human being in ChroD (ie, everyone except Prometheans and Demons) could be considered a Deviant, it's just that they've become common enough to create a set of shared characteristics. Like how one of the Requiem books speculates that the clans are technically unrelated types of vampiric beings that evolved convergently. And you could totally apply the Variation/Scar framework to other beings. Vampires have the Scars that they need blood and can't stand sunlight and so on. Mages are scarred in that they're driven by obsessions and their powers risk causing damage to reality (plus, the Power=Size and strength of the conspiracy chasing you fits Mages vs. Seers well). <br /> <br /> And I mentioned Host as being something I hope is a Clade, because it's so well represented in the source material and so wonderfully ripe for horror. Plus it's flexible- you could use it represent an alien parasite, a sapient nanomachine colony, or becoming the vessel for an ancient god. <br /> <br /> The &quot;no fuel stat&quot; thing is cool, and I can't wait to see it play out. I think that you could add a fuel stat as a Scar- have it be that the Deviant's powers rely on a limited pool of energy that they need to replenish some how. Another cool Scar would be that the Deviant only has access to their powers when in some sort of &quot;super&quot; mode, and you can add on drawbacks from there: it might have a limited duration, changing might be extremely painful, or the super mode might be so monstrous that it's impossible to socialize while in it. You could use that to represent a Deviant whose powers come from powered armor, actually. Though I'm also going to homebrew powered armor made from Deviants that lets them access some of the power of a Blowout without blowing up. I know this could unbalance it, but it's being planned as an optional thing ST's can throw in if they want to change the power level without actually having to alter the base mechanics. <br /> <br /> As an aside, I LOVE the Variation/Scar mechanics. It's the single most elegant way I've seen to sum up what it means to play a superhuman character in a horror setting- all power is inherently dangerous and dehumanizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-18-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T04:50:52-07:00","id":990368,"title":"","content":"Transformation sequences are reoccuring thing in the source material, especially the superheroish edge like Guyver, Blue Beetle (based on Guyver), Hulk, etc.<br /> <br /> The way we're currently handling it is not to have a supermode like Demon and Changeling2e; rather, there will be a variation that supresses other variations while active, along with their scars. When that power turns off, your true form reppears.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, Bruce Banner does not have a Variation of &quot;grow big and green when angry&quot;. Hulk has a Variation of &quot;turn off size increase and strength increase, with their associated beserk rage and inhuman appearance scars, as long as you remain calm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a fine difference, but an important one for our themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:14:03-07:00","id":990398,"title":"","content":"Every time you use the Hulk as an example I think back to the old TV series and crave Deviant a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:47:54-07:00","id":990406,"title":"","content":"Oooooh, that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:42:16-07:00","id":990994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=990368#post990368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transformation sequences are reoccuring thing in the source material, especially the superheroish edge like Guyver, Blue Beetle (based on Guyver), Hulk, etc.<br /> <br /> The way we're currently handling it is not to have a supermode like Demon and Changeling2e; rather, there will be a variation that supresses other variations while active, along with their scars. When that power turns off, your true form reppears.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, Bruce Banner does not have a Variation of &quot;grow big and green when angry&quot;. Hulk has a Variation of &quot;turn off size increase and strength increase, with their associated beserk rage and inhuman appearance scars, as long as you remain calm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a fine difference, but an important one for our themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, so the devinat state is your natural state? You're inhuman and the struggle is to remain human? I love it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:57:43-07:00","id":991003,"title":"","content":"Yeah. We want to have transforming characters as they're so prominent in the inspirations, but to have them be optional. Deviant is, ultimately, about playing the now-inhuman monster, so it becomes less &quot;you have a superform&quot; as &quot;you have a disguise&quot;. Active rather than passive camouflage. <br /> <br /> Plus this way, if anyone hits a transforming Remade with one of those &quot;your active powers turn off&quot; effects so beloved of crossover material, they're in for a nasty surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:47:42-07:00","id":991132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=991003#post991003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. We want to have transforming characters as they're so prominent in the inspirations, but to have them be optional. Deviant is, ultimately, about playing the now-inhuman monster, so it becomes less &quot;you have a superform&quot; as &quot;you have a disguise&quot;. Active rather than passive camouflage.<br /> <br /> Plus this way, if anyone hits a transforming Remade with one of those &quot;your active powers turn off&quot; effects so beloved of crossover material, they're in for a nasty surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be fun to play with.<br /> <br /> &quot;It looks like he's got some kind of magical disguise. I'm going to try and dispel it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You succeed in unraveling it. Now there's a pissed-off crocodile-man with foot-long claws, standing in front of you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:52:09-07:00","id":991136,"title":"","content":"The Remade are sounding better with every post I read about this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:14:54-07:00","id":992003,"title":"","content":"Unfh. It's everything I was trying to do with Pathogen and failed utterly. The kickstarter can't come soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:14:34-07:00","id":992049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=992003#post992003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfh. It's everything I was trying to do with Pathogen and failed utterly. The kickstarter can't come soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's any consolation, you did it before them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:56:53-07:00","id":992435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=992003#post992003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfh. It's everything I was trying to do with Pathogen and failed utterly. The kickstarter can't come soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, with a side of Yes smothered in a wonderful YEASS! sauce, but with the holidays coming I am not sure we'll see it before Febuary (but if a certain Dev wants to refute using dates and such - by all means).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:19:19-07:00","id":992493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=992435#post992435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, with a side of Yes smothered in a wonderful YEASS! sauce, but with the holidays coming I am not sure we'll see it before Febuary (but if a certain Dev wants to refute using dates and such - by all means).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich has said the KS for Prince's Gambit (Masquerade card game) is planned later this year (which schedule-wise means it's going to be the last one this year).<br /> <br /> Deviant's going to be a while, since it's not in first draft yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:55:14-07:00","id":992677,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Pathogen, I occasionally look wistfully at Virus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:23:57-07:00","id":993838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=981466#post981466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the rather excellent Jekyll (BBC show with James Nesbit) considered as source for Deviant. Elements are there, experiment and backlash against a controlling organization but spaced out since the experiment actually happened to the MCs progenitor</div> </div> </div> </div>Very late reply to this but yes, back in this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=948527#post948527\">post</a> that was quoted some of the inspirational media, Jekyll gets a mention. Which is excellent. Dealing with your super powered evil side sounds very Deviant indeed. I suppose your Tom Jackman/Hyde types might be Psychic, for the personality split, but then there wasn't common psychic phenomena in that series.<br /> <br /> I know it's marked for its similarities to Geist and Sin-Eaters but playing a Persona-user, particularly for all the problems and underlying conspiracy in Persona 3, would be a delicious Deviant game. <br /> <br /> The first batch of characters I'll stat up once Deviant is out will be inspired by a classic piece of children's literature. I'll have to go find the thread for initial character/conspiracy ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:34:04-07:00","id":994186,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming that, while Deviant creation is flexible and &quot;one-off unique freak&quot; shows up a lot, there will still be support for, I guess, &quot;breeds&quot; of Deviant, that all arose from the same experiment or similar procedures. Having all the players coming from the same conspiracy would help simplify things. It's in the source material, too, and there's a lot of potential there: having the characters fight Loyalist Deviants made using them same procedure or a more advanced one is something that's shown up in a lot of inspiration. I'm not talking about changing how Clades work or introducing another splat axis, more like having multiple Deviants of the psychic Clade all produced by the Ludevic Procedure or multiple cyborgs all created for Project Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:08:16-07:00","id":994210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=994186#post994186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming that, while Deviant creation is flexible and &quot;one-off unique freak&quot; shows up a lot, there will still be support for, I guess, &quot;breeds&quot; of Deviant, that all arose from the same experiment or similar procedures. Having all the players coming from the same conspiracy would help simplify things. It's in the source material, too, and there's a lot of potential there: having the characters fight Loyalist Deviants made using them same procedure or a more advanced one is something that's shown up in a lot of inspiration. I'm not talking about changing how Clades work or introducing another splat axis, more like having multiple Deviants of the psychic Clade all produced by the Ludevic Procedure or multiple cyborgs all created for Project Aegis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, or people stolen away and permanently mutated by inhuman fairy masters, or people warped into part-wolf spirit hunters by an insane moon-spirit-god, or people whose souls were moerged with a ghost and are wanted by the lords of the underworld, or intenseley powerful mummified servants of mysterious death gods, or blood-drinking parasites that must balance the inhuman beast in their souls with the constant game of political chess in which they must participate, or individuals awakened to the truths of reality who are locked in eternal conflict with servants of the platonic ideals of tyranny, or animated subhuman corpses whose souls are filled with a toxic divine fire, or the fallen servants of an unfeeling mechanistic God.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it could be relatively easy to hack Deviant into almost every other gameline. I love it because I love hacking gamelines to be each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:27:44-07:00","id":994240,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, I've on the &quot;technically any formerly human supernatural is a deviant&quot; thing, and it's a cool idea and I can't wait to go nuts with crossovers, but I was talking more about a more limited sort of group. Like, for example, how there are multiple clones in Orphan Black created by the same conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:57:22-07:00","id":994328,"title":"","content":"This looks really cool. Looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> My first thought when reading the description was Firestarter, which I had just read a few weeks ago.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T06:16:06-08:00","id":1002195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=990368#post990368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, put another way, Bruce Banner does not have a Variation of &quot;grow big and green when angry&quot;. Hulk has a Variation of &quot;turn off size increase and strength increase, with their associated beserk rage and inhuman appearance scars, as long as you remain calm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a fine difference, but an important one for our themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. How would this apply to Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde, where both forms were human, and neither had special powers?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:45:01-08:00","id":1002213,"title":"","content":"Given the way they are presented, most of the members of the Avengers in the MCU could be interpreted as Deviants in one form or another. Captain America underwent the Super Soldier treatment and now has Variations that grant him peak physical abilities, and his Scars are basically PTSD and survivor's guilt about WWII. Iron Man is a cyborg, and the arc reactor is his Scar, especially given the events of Iron Man 2, when he's slowly dying of radiation poisoning from the isotope in the arc reactor. Black Widow is a rather low-level Deviant who was initially a Loyalist, but went Renegade or joined another Organization (S.H.I.E.L.D.), and her Scars are the medical procedures the Red Room performed on her. The Hulk, we've already been over. Scarlet Witch and Quick Silver were volunteers who got major psychic powers and super speed, respectively. Spider-Man got bit by the Spider, and the Green Goblin is a Loyalist trying to track him down if you squint enough. Ant-Man... well, it all comes from the suit, so maybe? <br /> <br /> Everybody else seems to be a different splat. Hawkeye and Falcon are Hunters, maybe Task Force: VALKYRIE. Thor's straight out of Scion. The Vision... an Unfleshed Promethean, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:15:07-08:00","id":1002273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1002195#post1002195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. How would this apply to Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde, where both forms were human, and neither had special powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (the original versions) are applicable in Deviant. I think they'd be better represented by a single Merit. But if one looks at all the adaptations where Mr Hyde has super strength and/or other superpowers, Mr Hyde would be the actual character with Dr Jekyll being the other form, similarly to the Hulk and Bruce Banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:34:19-08:00","id":1002334,"title":"","content":"I wonder. I'm thinking of Orphan Black, which has been cited as a Deviant source, and the clones have low-level powers if they have them at all (fast healing, enhanced strength). I could see the original Jekyll and Hyde fitting, with transformation as their power, and Hyde perhaps manifesting enhanced strength. Basically at the weakest end of the Deviant spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T23:08:54-08:00","id":1002468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1002273#post1002273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (the original versions) are applicable in Deviant. I think they'd be better represented by a single Merit. But if one looks at all the adaptations where Mr Hyde has super strength and/or other superpowers, Mr Hyde would be the actual character with Dr Jekyll being the other form, similarly to the Hulk and Bruce Banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most versions of Mr. Hyde\u200b possess some degree of superhuman strength. The dissociative personality disorder would probably be the Scar. <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/mr-hyde/4005-3233/\" target=\"_blank\">Marvel's Mr. Hyde</a> is basically a mini-Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T00:15:15-08:00","id":1002474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1002213#post1002213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the way they are presented, most of the members of the Avengers in the MCU could be interpreted as Deviants in one form or another. Captain America underwent the Super Soldier treatment and now has Variations that grant him peak physical abilities, and his Scars are basically PTSD and survivor's guilt about WWII. Iron Man is a cyborg, and the arc reactor is his Scar, especially given the events of Iron Man 2, when he's slowly dying of radiation poisoning from the isotope in the arc reactor. Black Widow is a rather low-level Deviant who was initially a Loyalist, but went Renegade or joined another Organization (S.H.I.E.L.D.), and her Scars are the medical procedures the Red Room performed on her. The Hulk, we've already been over. Scarlet Witch and Quick Silver were volunteers who got major psychic powers and super speed, respectively. Spider-Man got bit by the Spider, and the Green Goblin is a Loyalist trying to track him down if you squint enough. Ant-Man... well, it all comes from the suit, so maybe?<br /> <br /> Everybody else seems to be a different splat. Hawkeye and Falcon are Hunters, maybe Task Force: VALKYRIE. Thor's straight out of Scion. The Vision... an Unfleshed Promethean, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go by the comics, then it works, since he shrinks and grows via the Pym Particles, which after repeated exposure he (and Janet, aka the Wasp) produce on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:07:40-08:00","id":1002971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Tessie:</b> I don't think Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (the original versions) are applicable in Deviant. I think they'd be better represented by a single Merit. </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, it could be said that Hyde has preternatural powers of persuasion: the first we see of him, he's talking down an angry mob who saw him trample a little girl; and despite everyone hating him at first sight he rarely has much trouble getting people to do what he wants. So maybe he has a Variation of super-charisma, with a Scar of engendering hatred whenever he's not actively engaging in persuasion. Assuming Variations and Scars lean that social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:39:26-08:00","id":1013124,"title":"","content":"I really want rules for a hive mind entity in deviant. 5 PCs having to coexist in each others heads<br /> <br /> Any new info? Schpoiluhs? Cuz,you know - we all got needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:55:40-08:00","id":1013127,"title":"","content":"I'm calling such ReMade &quot;Amalgams&quot; for the moment, but I don't know if there'll be room for them in the corebook or if they'll have to wait until later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:00:34-08:00","id":1013130,"title":"","content":"Oh, wait - did you mean a group of Remade who are networked together, Sense8 style? That's just a Variation. Amalgams (name very temp) are when a Deviant used to be more than one person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby