6-ameraaaaaa","user":"Ameraaaaaa","date":".  i sald 5 feet but i meant 50 feet 05-28-2017, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:12:02-07:00","id":1097722,"title":"","content":"Well a character that giant is probably not going to be allowed since it breaks the masquerade so severely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:36:17-07:00","id":1097732,"title":"","content":"I always envisioned this game to be one that doesn't care about a Masquerade so much.<br /> <br /> By default, your Variants and Scars are visible (if physical). They only are hidden when you have a Variant that 'turns off' your powers or Scars. Secondly, and in a twist, I think it would be the <i>Conspiracies</i> interested in upholding a Masquerade since they're generally 'normal' organizations. The Remade Renegades, however, would probably love to blow the lid on nebulous organizations that create horrifying cyborgs. Their only hesitation, and only reason for upholding a Masquerade, is they don't want the Conspiracies to know where they are and come right after them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise a 50 foot woman is a very interesting character and a good example of the Remade for all the reasons the Hulk is: dare I use my powers which are super obvious and paint a bulls eye on me, or do I hide from my enemies and live in fear forever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T05:12:25-07:00","id":1097752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1097732#post1097732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always envisioned this game to be one that doesn't care about a Masquerade so much.<br /> <br /> By default, your Variants and Scars are visible (if physical). They only are hidden when you have a Variant that 'turns off' your powers or Scars. Secondly, and in a twist, I think it would be the <i>Conspiracies</i> interested in upholding a Masquerade since they're generally 'normal' organizations. The Remade Renegades, however, would probably love to blow the lid on nebulous organizations that create horrifying cyborgs. Their only hesitation, and only reason for upholding a Masquerade, is they don't want the Conspiracies to know where they are and come right after them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise a 50 foot woman is a very interesting character and a good example of the Remade for all the reasons the Hulk is: dare I use my powers which are super obvious and paint a bulls eye on me, or do I hide from my enemies and live in fear forever?</div> </div> </div> </div>plus 50 foot woman is a fameus horrer movie monster even though i,ve never seen it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T14:49:11-07:00","id":1097873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1097732#post1097732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always envisioned this game to be one that doesn't care about a Masquerade so much.<br /> <br /> By default, your Variants and Scars are visible (if physical). They only are hidden when you have a Variant that 'turns off' your powers or Scars. Secondly, and in a twist, I think it would be the <i>Conspiracies</i> interested in upholding a Masquerade since they're generally 'normal' organizations. The Remade Renegades, however, would probably love to blow the lid on nebulous organizations that create horrifying cyborgs. Their only hesitation, and only reason for upholding a Masquerade, is they don't want the Conspiracies to know where they are and come right after them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise a 50 foot woman is a very interesting character and a good example of the Remade for all the reasons the Hulk is: dare I use my powers which are super obvious and paint a bulls eye on me, or do I hide from my enemies and live in fear forever?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a very big difference between &quot;Scars which can probably be hidden by clothes&quot; and &quot;Look I'm as tall as a skyscraper and everyone can see me and thousands of people are now filming me with their phones&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, if a player was at that scale.... wouldn't it basically become freeform considering how much you'd have to screw with the strength and hitpoint rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:12:20-07:00","id":1097883,"title":"","content":"I think the closest one could pull off the concept is playing an Anakim in Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:09:19-07:00","id":1097949,"title":"","content":"But now she a 50 foot woman so it should be fine<br /> plus i might still give her the power to shrink down just it in case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T21:00:17-07:00","id":1097967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1097873#post1097873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a very big difference between &quot;Scars which can probably be hidden by clothes&quot; and &quot;Look I'm as tall as a skyscraper and everyone can see me and thousands of people are now filming me with their phones&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, if a player was at that scale.... wouldn't it basically become freeform considering how much you'd have to screw with the strength and hitpoint rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. There is a very big difference there, which is why that wasn't the example I gave:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/13/135116/2979148-hulktoobig2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> At any rate, Deviant is still a game where you can blow out into a cathedral of flesh so I'm not sure why there's any debate if you can turn into a 50 foot woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T22:09:39-07:00","id":1097983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1097967#post1097967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. There is a very big difference there, which is why that wasn't the example I gave:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/13/135116/2979148-hulktoobig2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> At any rate, Deviant is still a game where you can blow out into a cathedral of flesh so I'm not sure why there's any debate if you can turn into a 50 foot woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I wasn't saying the issue was with the hulk. It's &quot;your asking for a character ten times the size of hulk, and expecting the setting to not break&quot;. Yes, both of the character concepts have the risk of &quot;the more I'm seen in my giant form the easier it is for the evil people to find me&quot;, but that doesn't actually resolve the issue being discussed at all.<br /> <br /> Also cathedral of flesh doesn't actually denote any certain size, I mean you can have those which only take up a room. And wasn't the mention of that with the blowouts? So it'd be a one time dramatic &quot;holy shit&quot; moment not &quot;every week&quot; and no one ever seems to notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T22:44:30-07:00","id":1097990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1097983#post1097983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also cathedral of flesh doesn't actually denote any certain size, I mean you can have those which only take up a room. And wasn't the mention of that with the blowouts? So it'd be a one time dramatic &quot;holy shit&quot; moment not &quot;every week&quot; and no one ever seems to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all completely fair. To clarify, I wasn't saying &quot;cathedral of flesh&quot; is about size (but...wasn't it? It consumed a city) but it's of comparable extremes: blowing out to a nuclear degree and becoming as tall as a skyscraper.<br /> <br /> So yeah, when I did write that I was imagining the poster's character concept as, &quot;Gains Giant merit as a suppressible Variant but can Blow Out to 50 foot woman.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:31:03-07:00","id":1097995,"title":"","content":"not the giant merit <br /> inseed its 50 foot suppressibie and blow out to skyscraper <br /> i think since most of the time blow out means death afterword a one time thing in the mountains can be covered up because even though many people that do see it will have to make people believe the its not photoshop on there phones and thats if the mountains are not covering her<br /> in the city though not so much since that many witnesses might brake the mask but then again thats not what keeps the mask its because most people know but they dont wanna look carzy plus monsters dont like being talked about plus its one city","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:26:56-07:00","id":1103460,"title":"","content":"Will the Deviant rules be able to model a group of folks who have been forcefully awakened to all of their past lives, some of whom now want to be the dominant personality. No Mythic superhuman abilities but a ton of skills and knowledges that they simply should not have according to their lifestyle.<br /> <br /> What would the Blowout of such a Deviant look like, since it's not going to be as flashy as the Cathedral of Flesh, except maybe to psychic perceptions?<br /> <br /> are we going to see the equivalent to ghouls or wolf-kin? Would love to see some &quot;normal&quot; psychic come into contact with a Deviant and just freak right the hell out. &quot;I seen some shit in my day. Ghosts walking endless strecthes of the same 5 feet. Leeches feeding on the dance floor. I even seen a man made of nothing but clockworks. But you, You are FUCTUP!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T23:41:21-07:00","id":1103734,"title":"","content":"that would be an awesome pc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T08:10:36-07:00","id":1105084,"title":"","content":"&quot;Normal&quot; psychics are already possible with the 2e core's supernatural merits. They cover aura reading, telekinesis, psychokinesis, and being a medium, off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> I imagine a psychic's blowout would be more like a Cronenberg head explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T13:58:55-07:00","id":1105170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105084#post1105084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Normal&quot; psychics are already possible with the 2e core's supernatural merits. They cover aura reading, telekinesis, psychokinesis, and being a medium, off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> I imagine a psychic's blowout would be more like a Cronenberg head explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Scanners explisions seem possible. Alternately, they could start to cause the laws of physics to break down in the area and/or tear a hole between the physical and a particularly nasty part of the Astral.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of realizing that it's kind of possible that the earliest members of certain splats could have possibly been Deviants originally. Hypothetically, they could well have all had Deviant progenitors, including Beasts, which would be kind of funny if that turned out to be the case and a Beast found out. Just, &quot;Wait, so my people are just a branch, and <i>these guys</i> are the original monsters? Ugh, by the Dark Mother, I'm gonna need a drink.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:28:27-07:00","id":1105681,"title":"","content":"&quot;&quot;Born with it&quot; is one of the Origins (x-splats) for Deviant, covering everything from Orphan Black to the Innsmouth Look.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw in the <b>Mutations causing superhuman mortals?</b><br /><br /> thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T08:43:28-07:00","id":1105711,"title":"","content":"Really well awesome now xmen time except xmen dont have as much scars so yeah just give them dread powers and there all hunted by the government and only few are high powered but hey not everything translates perfectly or even at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:02:56-07:00","id":1105718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105711#post1105711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really well awesome now xmen time except xmen dont have as much scars so yeah just give them dread powers and there all hunted by the government and only few are high powered but hey not everything translates perfectly or even at all</div> </div> </div> </div>Xavier is paraplegic, Jean Grey has a superpowered evil persona (and we even see her Blowout by calling out the Phoenix), Rogue and Cyclops can't control their powers, Nightcrawler, Mystique, Toad and Beast have obviously inhuman apperances, and Wolverine's powers are slowly turning him into a feral animal. Those sound like Scars to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:09:05-07:00","id":1105750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105718#post1105718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Wolverine's powers are slowly turning him into a feral animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus he's wanted by various government organizations who are trying to turn him into a mind controlled weapon of mass destruction or just steal his adamantium. He's basically got two origins. So does Jean Grey, considering the Hellfire Club and other organizations and their obsessions over the Phoenix. And Cyclops! Not only dealing with the mutant hating public, but the manipulations of Mister Sinister to get his genetics. There's probably more examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-20-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:40:02-07:00","id":1105758,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't count social ramifications as Scars. But Cyclops <i>does</i> have the \u201ccan't open his eyes without destroying what he's looking at\u201d problem, just like Rogue can't touch anyone without traumatizing them (and herself). Jean Gray originally had a similar problem, where she didn't do well in crowds because it took effort to <i>not</i> read a mind, and a crowd would quickly overwhelm her. Storm was a claustrophobe. In other cases you have to dig to find the Scars (Iceman, for instance). <br /> <br /> Frankly, I think that a group of Deviants would have it worse than the X-Men, whose primary problem <i>was</i> social. I'd be more inclined to look at DC's Doom Patrol for Deviant material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:40:40-07:00","id":1105759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105750#post1105750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus he's wanted by various government organizations who are trying to turn him into a mind controlled weapon of mass destruction or just steal his adamantium. He's basically got two origins. So does Jean Grey, considering the Hellfire Club and other organizations and their obsessions over the Phoenix. And Cyclops! Not only dealing with the mutant hating public, but the manipulations of Mister Sinister to get his genetics. There's probably more examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scars! Scars everywhere!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:52:25-07:00","id":1105787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105758#post1105758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't count social ramifications as Scars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure they said at one point that people going after you was an option for a scar (like Eleven from stranger things having the government out to get her).<br /> <br /> I certainly hope it's like that. Simple drawbacks or physical mutations would suck. I want to play someone who looks completely normal, but everyone near her irrationally hates her (like a promethean) or who's got the secret service after her. That's a way better story than: 'I can't go out in public because I look like a cronenberg monster (although I love that idea as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:22:18-07:00","id":1105799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105787#post1105787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure they said at one point that people going after you was an option for a scar (like Eleven from stranger things having the government out to get her).</div> </div> </div> </div> If that's what they do, so be it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105787#post1105787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly hope it's like that. Simple drawbacks or physical mutations would suck. I want to play someone who looks completely normal, but everyone near her irrationally hates her (like a promethean) or who's got the secret service after her. That's a way better story than: 'I can't go out in public because I look like a cronenberg monster (although I love that idea as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that you wouldn't be able to tell stories centered around social ramifications; that would be stupid. I just don't see how they could be Scars, as Scars are (as I understand them) intimately linked to how pretty your Variations are: your Variation becomes more potent, and your Scar automatically becomes more intense; your Variation weakens, and your Scar automatically subsides. That's what sets Scars apart from regular Complications: they are harmful manifestations of the same cracked soul of which your Variations are helpful manifestations.<br /> <br /> That is, <b>Deviants</b> isn't designed to handle people whose <i>only</i> problems are social. There will always be some sort of physical, mental, or supernatural problems stemming from their powers that they have to deal with as well. <br /> <br /> Which, again, is not to say that there aren't social complications: the game is, after all, <b>Deviant: the Renegades</b> \u2014 you can't be a renegade without something to rebel against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:56:02-07:00","id":1105813,"title":"","content":"Linking them with Scars, if Scars are just what you say, was probably the wrong way to go about it. But Deviant isn't just about living with some weird gimmick, which any supernatural template has, it also has an emphasis on people or organizations coming after you. There, the X-men shine, both individually with groups like the Hellfire Club who see you as the harbinger of their Phoenix figure or Mister Sinister who wants your genetic potential, and as a group, with the Reavers and other mutant-hating groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T16:31:38-07:00","id":1105866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105799#post1105799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If that's what they do, so be it.<br /> <br /> I never said that you wouldn't be able to tell stories centered around social ramifications; that would be stupid. I just don't see how they could be Scars, as Scars are (as I understand them) intimately linked to how pretty your Variations are: your Variation becomes more potent, and your Scar automatically becomes more intense; your Variation weakens, and your Scar automatically subsides. That's what sets Scars apart from regular Complications: they are harmful manifestations of the same cracked soul of which your Variations are helpful manifestations.<br /> <br /> That is, <b>Deviants</b> isn't designed to handle people whose <i>only</i> problems are social. There will always be some sort of physical, mental, or supernatural problems stemming from their powers that they have to deal with as well.<br /> <br /> Which, again, is not to say that there aren't social complications: the game is, after all, <b>Deviant: the Renegades</b> \u2014 you can't be a renegade without something to rebel against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, apologies, I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to this game. Does anyone know if they are planning to do a kickstarter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T21:15:59-07:00","id":1105934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105866#post1105866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, apologies, I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to this game. Does anyone know if they are planning to do a kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so. I like OP's kickstarters. I pledged in two of them, and was very pleased with the results each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T21:35:38-07:00","id":1105939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105934#post1105934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope so. I like OP's kickstarters. I pledged in two of them, and was very pleased with the results each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. It would be cool for the core, give them a view of how many people like it and so potentially more books, or at least know what kind of books people want. Would be nice to have a deluxe edition of this new game as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T02:10:37-07:00","id":1105982,"title":"","content":"I hope they don't make all the organizations purely evil. A couple with more gray morals would be great. For example, maybe the religious cult has used you to become the avatar of their god to prevent another one from destroying the world, or perhaps the military has turned you into a cyborg because they need super soldiers to fight off a secret extradimensional invasion. What they've done to you is still morally wrong, but at least you can understand why they did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T02:25:20-07:00","id":1105983,"title":"","content":"Nah mayb for some people and i can maybe try it my self but a purely evil group lets me go on a justified roaring rampage of revenge but both I'd like for there own purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T06:26:05-07:00","id":1106025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105982#post1105982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they don't make all the organizations purely evil. A couple with more gray morals would be great. For example, maybe the religious cult has used you to become the avatar of their god to prevent another one from destroying the world, or perhaps the military has turned you into a cyborg because they need super soldiers to fight off a secret extradimensional invasion. What they've done to you is still morally wrong, but at least you can understand why they did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Arthur, I agree, it's pretty fucked that we're trying to take your bone marrow, but this will cure, <i>at the least</i>, cancer, AIDS and the common cold. Possibly death itself. And if you're not going to cooperate, then I'm sorry, dude, but we gotta take it. I'll make sure your family gets a portion of the proceeds.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T06:51:43-07:00","id":1106030,"title":"","content":"Those are a bit much. How fun would it be to play a character whose concept is, 'Kill yourself or the world ends.' Every choice you made besides turning yourself in is pure selfishness. Plus you would never be able to justify it to anyone. 'Well, I didn't want my family and everything I loved to end, but I understand the hobo life is for you and you don't like the government. No hard feelings about stealing my money, either, a hobo's gotta eat, right?'<br /> <br /> It's still the Chronicles of Darkness, nothing is so objectively good or evil, or right.<br /> <br /> It's probably the kind of thing you could homebrew but come on. You really want those as one of the primary options? Besides, if it was a matter of life and death for the entire world wouldn't it be likely they could find someone completely willing to do it? Even if it was a matter of 'you are the only one capable of doing this,' for such a grand and necessary goal it seems like they'd, you know, ask you about it first so you didn't wake up, freak out and run.<br /> <br /> At least dim it down to things like the other god not flat out about to destroy the world but, perhaps, destroying their religion. Or not a definitive invasion but 'just in case' such a thing ever happens. And some more indefinite 'we <i>might </i>be able to put your marrow to good use,' rather than 'yes we can definitely cure all these bad things if you just let us cut you open. And yes please don't concern yourself that our bosses are the wealthiest and oldest men in the world, having invested heavily in pharmaceuticals, they're definitely going to share the discoveries they make off your body.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2017, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:18:03-07:00","id":1106040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106025#post1106025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Arthur, I agree, it's pretty fucked that we're trying to take your bone marrow, but this will cure, <i>at the least</i>, cancer, AIDS and the common cold. Possibly death itself. And if you're not going to cooperate, then I'm sorry, dude, but we gotta take it. I'll make sure your family gets a portion of the proceeds.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, this made me laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:19:42-07:00","id":1106041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106030#post1106030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are a bit much. How fun would it be to play a character whose concept is, 'Kill yourself or the world ends.' Every choice you made besides turning yourself in is pure selfishness. Plus you would never be able to justify it to anyone. 'Well, I didn't want my family and everything I loved to end, but I understand the hobo life is for you and you don't like the government. No hard feelings about stealing my money, either, a hobo's gotta eat, right?'<br /> <br /> It's still the Chronicles of Darkness, nothing is so objectively good or evil, or right.<br /> <br /> It's probably the kind of thing you could homebrew but come on. You really want those as one of the primary options? Besides, if it was a matter of life and death for the entire world wouldn't it be likely they could find someone completely willing to do it? Even if it was a matter of 'you are the only one capable of doing this,' for such a grand and necessary goal it seems like they'd, you know, ask you about it first so you didn't wake up, freak out and run.<br /> <br /> At least dim it down to things like the other god not flat out about to destroy the world but, perhaps, destroying their religion. Or not a definitive invasion but 'just in case' such a thing ever happens. And some more indefinite 'we <i>might </i>be able to put your marrow to good use,' rather than 'yes we can definitely cure all these bad things if you just let us cut you open. And yes please don't concern yourself that our bosses are the wealthiest and oldest men in the world, having invested heavily in pharmaceuticals, they're definitely going to share the discoveries they make off your body.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes I hear what you're saying. I may have gone a bit too far with my examples, yours are way better. The real reason I wanted to talk about grey organizations was to discuss about loyalists. What are the reasons that compel them to stay with the organization that made them deviants in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:43:30-07:00","id":1106051,"title":"","content":"Oh I've faith that there will be some reasons to join the loyalists. At the very least, we've been told that Deviants can be a danger to people around them. I imagine there will be a sliding scale in the organizations, with some goals being more morally justified, even if not something the entire world would get behind. And even among loyalists you could probably have one guy who's willing to destroy everything in their way to the target, and another who doesn't want any collateral.<br /> <br /> Though the emphasis is still probably going to be on Renegades at first. I think we've been told that loyalists won't be expanded upon in the core book, but it's been a while. There'll even probably be ways to go from one side to another, with Loyalists going Renegade, and Renegades going Loyalist.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/z03notk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is Michael Cray, Codename: Deathblow. He's a hitter for a top secret organization, and just found out he has an inoperable tumor in his head. They've asked him for one last job and, not being given all the information on the target, he does a little digging and finds out that not only is this target not 'good' meaning not justified, and as he puts it to his boss, 'Do I have to start worrying abotu some of my other missions? Have I just discovered, right at the end of my goddamn life, that you've been playing me for years?'<br /> <br /> I fully expect we'll find that the tumor is not a tumor and he's going to become a major thorn in the side of his former employers.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T08:16:43-07:00","id":1106063,"title":"","content":"Could a Renegade have more than one Org? Like, say you have one Org that wants to use them to power their future city, and another want to use them to summon their eldritch gods, and they're both after him, and may cooperate or clash as appropriate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:35:46-07:00","id":1106131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106063#post1106063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Renegade have more than one Org? Like, say you have one Org that wants to use them to power their future city, and another want to use them to summon their eldritch gods, and they're both after him, and may cooperate or clash as appropriate?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7ejsM0VF-Os\" target=\"_blank\">Soundtrack to this.</a><br /> <br /> <b>The Disaster of Project Yoon-Sun</b><br /> <br /> The United States Special Interests Research and Training unit (SPIRTAI) was a joint division between the United States Army Intelligence and Security Command (INSCOM), United States Army recruiting command (USAREC), United States Army Test and Evaluation Command (ATEC), United States Military Academy (USMA), The Air Force Research Laboratory (AFRL), and overseen by the Marine Special Operations command (USSOCOM). SPIRTAI's main function is to promote bright students and young military personnel into special groups that function as &quot;Think Tanks&quot; to solve many problems in the military either as a whole or specific cases. The groups created were not at all dissimilar to several Gifted Educational programs in elementary and post elementary schools. <br /> <br /> While the division focused on the creation of fresh innovation across the broad spectrum military Academics and special developments, by 1973 the need for the inclusion of private military contractors due to a steady decline in budget for this area of the military. With the inclusion of private contractors, the division suffered a confusion due to several reorganizations and HR complaints on some of the research and tasks requested of the Think Tanks involved resulted in the division being quietly and largely disbanded with the only remnant being the remaining Think Tank group and it's associate project (would come to be known as Yoon-Sun after one of the members of the group) which continued it's study under the watch of Three generals that composed the decision making party of SPIRTAI, the funding of the Federal Special Interests Group (FESIG), and personnel/resources of Limited Ltd. (a business with several companies but prides itself in training and scouting programs for schools, other companies, the military, and governmental positions).<br /> <br /> Project Yoon-Sun revolved around the idea of helping Air-Force pilots withstand greater g-force pressures and other related hazards to protect the pilots and soldiers in duty. The group found many possibilities in certain types of people if born in certain kinds of hypothetical environments or stresses. All of it theoretical to them but their research was in how technology could be created to emulate the types of protections that pilots would need. Over the course of their research they concluded that there could be similar technologies that might help soldiers in other divisions. Not told to the Think Tank, an illegal Human Research group created by FESIG and Limited LTD under the command of the corrupt Generals of SPIRTAI had been carrying out illegal human experimentation using the findings, research, and ideas of the Think Tanks for its entire run. The Most successful became Project Yoon-Sun which genetically engineered what the differring parties hoped would be the ideal test subject for use in enhancing various military personnel. <br /> <br /> After several failed attempts, a child of Project Yoon-Sun survived the engineering and mechanical process. The Child grew in the care of the personnel of the engineers. The child did not meet anyone of their age and mostly consisted of tests after test. The child did not age the same as would be expected. Over time, a well meaning but ultimately extreme group calling themselves The Unification Corps heard of Project Yoon-Sun and attempted to embed themselves in the organization that studied the Child in an attempt to free them. On the Child's technical 18th birthday, the Corps attempted to break the child out. While they were successful in that the Child escaped, everyone present save for a few, died. Survivors report that the Child became unstable during this time. <br /> <br /> With the Child on the run and attempting to find out more about themselves as well as the outside world, several groups are now both on a hunt and a race. The three generals want to recover the Child for their climb to the tops of the military political ladder as well as the Child's obvious application on the soldiers of the battlefield. FESIG wants the child back as they consider the Child to be technically fully funded by them and the escape created a possible loss of monetary assets if seized by anyone else. Limited Ltd. cannot allow the Child to be caught or seen outside of a laboratory for the research they conducted and how it may help many of their goals, chief among them the Recruitment program. And finally the The Unification Corps, while well meaning, see the Child as the ultimate weapon to be hurled at their enemies, specifically the military. <br /> <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">tl;dr: I def see a Renegade with more than one Org... and I think I may have just created my character for when it comes out<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> XD</span></b></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:21:01-07:00","id":1106194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106131#post1106131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>And were this a video game, one scene/stage near the end would involve a massive 4-way pile up, with you/the Child navigating the Chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:19:26-07:00","id":1106311,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that Deviant orgs are going to be user-defined; that is, part of designing your Deviant will involve designing the organization that made you what you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:25:10-07:00","id":1106313,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Cheiron Group from HtV explicitly mentioned as one of the possible organisations? If there's rules for creating your own antagonistic organisations it's probably going to be in addition to predefined ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:51:05-07:00","id":1106324,"title":"","content":"No; DaveB mentioned at one point that he was hoping that Cheiron Group ought to be an option. This is consistent with the idea that roles for creating your own organization is the main option, in that you can use such rules to define Cheiron Group if you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T20:23:04-07:00","id":1106392,"title":"","content":"Hate the song but love the group and the player character but 1 thing so hes immune high pressure but has the body of a kid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:04:55-07:00","id":1106550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106392#post1106392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate the song but love the group and the player character but 1 thing so hes immune high pressure but has the body of a kid</div> </div> </div> </div>I left most of it ambiguous so that you could make the Child with more or less any power with some justification (depending how powers are chosen in D:tR). The project started with that goal but over time found other applications of the same scenario. <br /> <br /> For example, I used all neutral pronouns because if I were to play The Child she would be of my own gender and I'd prolly like her to have interesting damage immunizations through quantum fluctuations or some such cause that sounds pretty cool to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:34:43-07:00","id":1106574,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhhhhh that makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:00:03-07:00","id":1106674,"title":"","content":"Is Frankenstein's monster a Deviant? <br /> <br /> He has scars (literally and abandonment issues, for figuratively). <br /> He was experimented on (being patchworked back to life). <br /> He has someone who is chasing him who he is rebelling against (Frankenstein chases him into the icy north doesn't he? I know it small but an organization could very well be one very driven nemisis, I think)<br /> In many tellings he has superhuman powers ranging from abnormal strength to control of electricity and lightning<br /> One of the pillars of the mythology around him is how his inability to connect to people around him drives him mad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:08:48-07:00","id":1106675,"title":"","content":"He could be. More obviously, he's a Promethean. The idea is Prometheans are soulless, life-filled things searching to be whole. A Deviant version of Frankenstein's monster would be more played straight as a hunted and vengeful pseudo-man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:48:30-07:00","id":1106856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106675#post1106675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could be. More obviously, he's a Promethean. The idea is Prometheans are soulless, life-filled things searching to be whole. A Deviant version of Frankenstein's monster would be more played straight as a hunted and vengeful pseudo-man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that Deviant might be a good solution for crossover play, much like Beast was. It just looks like it might be flexible enough to let players mix splats without actually &quot;mixing splats.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T03:28:54-07:00","id":1106940,"title":"","content":"Is deviant going to have some kind of metaplot? or are they going to let it entirely on our hands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T03:43:44-07:00","id":1106943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106940#post1106940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is deviant going to have some kind of metaplot? or are they going to let it entirely on our hands?</div> </div> </div> </div>The CofD hasn't had a metaplot yet, at least in the sense of advancing the present-day setting over time - the closest so far has been Mummy, which keeps expanding and developing its backstory, revealing more about Irem. Given Deviant seems to be exceedingly customisable, I'm not sure what a metaplot would look like.<br /> <br /> (There's also New Orleans in Vampire, but that was thanks to outside events.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T05:56:43-07:00","id":1106980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106674#post1106674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Frankenstein's monster a Deviant?<br /> <br /> He has scars (literally and abandonment issues, for figuratively).<br /> He was experimented on (being patchworked back to life).<br /> He has someone who is chasing him who he is rebelling against (Frankenstein chases him into the icy north doesn't he? I know it small but an organization could very well be one very driven nemisis, I think)<br /> In many tellings he has superhuman powers ranging from abnormal strength to control of electricity and lightning<br /> One of the pillars of the mythology around him is how his inability to connect to people around him drives him mad</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Promethean</b> is a game where you're created whole cloth as a monster and long to become human. <b>Deviant</b> is about being human and being made <i>into</i> a monster. You're not a lonely monster; you're isolated, but you have people you protect and people you take vengeance on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T05:56:45-07:00","id":1106981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106940#post1106940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is deviant going to have some kind of metaplot? or are they going to let it entirely on our hands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly doubtful (as stated by @marin).<br /> <br /> I'm interested to see what the sample and SASs might look like, though. Deviant seems the lend itself well to telling discrete stories (since them dying seems common enough to include rules/mention in the core).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-23-2017, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T21:20:51-07:00","id":1107204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1106943#post1106943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The CofD hasn't had a metaplot yet, at least in the sense of advancing the present-day setting over time - the closest so far has been Mummy, which keeps expanding and developing its backstory, revealing more about Irem. Given Deviant seems to be exceedingly customisable, I'm not sure what a metaplot would look like.<br /> <br /> (There's also New Orleans in Vampire, but that was thanks to outside events.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the same argument could be made for the Boston setting in Mage, though much of that is purely in the form of fiction pieces within the books (and thus optional for your game), and I'm not sure the Boston marathon bombings quite hit the same level as Katrina or 9/11 in terms of outside forces necessarily influencing the setting/story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:18:18-07:00","id":1107655,"title":"","content":"Besides, \u201cReal Life Intervenes\u201d isn't metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T11:18:12-07:00","id":1107688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1107655#post1107655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, \u201cReal Life Intervenes\u201d isn't metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or is it even more Meta meta-plot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","