row-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Mummy is yellow enough then I think Werewolf can be orange enough. I fear one day they will come out with a hot pink skull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Barbie: The Playing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T02:48:33-07:00","id":1123378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123341#post1123341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Mummy is yellow enough then I think Werewolf can be orange enough. I fear one day they will come out with a hot pink skull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Princess the Hopeful (the fan game-line)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:09:38-07:00","id":1123431,"title":"","content":"Ow I am so amazed with the new skull! I actually thought it will stay glowing aggresive orange - so more resembling Akira and anime supernatural stuff. But now it is dark red like VTR.. more into Fly direction. That's how it should feel. Every supernatural in WoD should make you feel as damned, not priviledged. And it will be uncomfortable to create weirdo like Fly one. That's it.<br /> Really waiting for sneaks of Variations, Origins, Clades &lt;3 And more artworks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:24:12-07:00","id":1123478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123378#post1123378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Princess the Hopeful (the fan game-line)?</div> </div> </div> </div>As unlikely as that would be due to innumerable copyright issues, I would be totally fine with ChroD incorporating Princess, using that very color.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:37:16-07:00","id":1123664,"title":"","content":"Nah. Pink is the colour of psychodelics and body (like Promethean) -&gt; Sanitarium. But we have Beast for stuff like nightmares","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T17:16:01-07:00","id":1123711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123664#post1123664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Pink is the colour of psychodelics and body (like Promethean) -&gt; Sanitarium. But we have Beast for stuff like nightmares</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose. For me, rainbows come to mind rather than any specific color for psychedelics.<br /> <br /> If we're on the tangent of colors for prospective gamelines, I wonder what other colors remain? Somebody mentioned orange, and we don't really have black or white either. I suppose I might change Geist to black and/or white just to differentiate it from Corebook blue, since Geist's only book is blue. If I were to make a gameline <i>just</i> for orange, I think we could go with a game centered around invasion horror. Maybe one about playing an interdimensional incursion? Pink I still think would go to Princess if it were canonized. Genius I would imagine as a sickly, paler green (as opposed to the dark green of Hunter). Promethean doesn't really have a &quot;color&quot; yet, at least, going by the covers. The Promethean books don't seem to have a single cominant color. I could be wrong though, it's been a while since' I've looked at my Promethean books and they're not with me right now.<br /> <br /> But back to the actual topic at hand, I actually look forward to rolling up darker versions of some of my Mutants and Masterminds characters. Particularly, I had a character who unwittingly had an infant god gestating in his soul, and it brought him back with a semi-random set of powers each time, as well as cutting out some of his humanity. It was neat when we played a sort of 2099-style game where he cropped up as an enemy and the immortal God-King of New Dallas in a possible bad future.<br /> <br /> Do you suppose powers can mutate and morph freely of the player's influence out of the box? Because that could be interesting, if perhaps hard to work with as an ST. And if it's not there to start it might not be too terribly hard to hack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T05:10:34-07:00","id":1123833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you suppose powers can mutate and morph freely of the player's influence out of the box? Because that could be interesting, if perhaps hard to work with as an ST. And if it's not there to start it might not be too terribly hard to hack. </div> </div> </div>Well I guess it should work like this. There should be some glitch/paradox way of twisting powers of Deviant if he's unlucky. That's his personal cancer. And that's the way I craeted Victors in Mage: The Ascension, sometimes their supplements gltiched (in magickal terms it was paradox reaction). Same with clones, cyborgs etc. Expecting same from Variations-Scars relationship. And that nothing feels safe as golden mean (like in others supernaturals who keep their Wyrd/Synergy etc. in safe number) - because it's hurt locker to live with Scars. Power at a price and feeling the victim all time. Without marysuistic &quot;he has nightmares&quot;.<br /> I'm waiting for abducted by UFO Deviant :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T20:20:59-07:00","id":1126942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1105813#post1105813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Linking them with Scars, if Scars are just what you say, was probably the wrong way to go about it. But Deviant isn't just about living with some weird gimmick, which any supernatural template has, it also has an emphasis on people or organizations coming after you. There, the X-men shine, both individually with groups like the Hellfire Club who see you as the harbinger of their Phoenix figure or Mister Sinister who wants your genetic potential, and as a group, with the Reavers and other mutant-hating groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically the Reavers are ALSO Deviants: being cyborgs, they would be a rival type of Remade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:06:47-07:00","id":1127207,"title":"","content":"There's a comics Kickstarter up that reads like the creator was trying to depict a Remaking, whether that were his intention or not:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1396425866/ferrofluid-issue-1?ref=recs_newest\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ef=recs_newest</a><br /> <br /> I may or may not back it myself, but I thought I'd share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:28:05-07:00","id":1128839,"title":"","content