ack. (that nip, man. It's a problem)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">And here it is: the first inaugural blog post solely about Deviant.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:46:26-07:00","id":1130118,"title":"","content":"Guardians and Nemesises sound very intriguing. I'm also pretty excited to see how Deviant interacts with Mage in DE2. It will be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:53:55-07:00","id":1130123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130118#post1130118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians and Nemesises sound very intriguing. I'm also pretty excited to see how Deviant interacts with Mage in DE2. It will be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on both points, though I'm even more excited to see the Deviant/Hunter interaction line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T23:29:49-07:00","id":1130159,"title":"","content":"I just now want to try some ideas<br /> Someone who can see the future but only a few seconds but has unusual eyes <br /> Someone 10 foot big with super strength and durability <br /> Someone who can rearrange atoms but thinks extremely different so maybe everything they do needs to roll for wether they do it or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13426,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","user":"Ameraaaaaa","date":". 08-19-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T23:51:47-07:00","id":1130163,"title":"","content":"My main hunger is for some examples of Clades and Origins that get away from the sci-fi/cyberpunk source material that's more readily at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:09:00-07:00","id":1130180,"title":"","content":"I believe the revealed origins so far are accident, birth (in vivo?). My guess infection, surgury, fantastical for the rest. <br /> <br /> Clades Part Machine, Psionic, Animal Hybrid, guesses for the rest Mutation (the Hulk, jekle and Hyde) and Ritualist. <br /> <br /> Symbionant I think will be a variation for Animal Hybrid, not a clade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:10:40-07:00","id":1130181,"title":"","content":"Perhaps in an expansion I'd love to see Possessed reimagined as a Deviant Clade, with vices as variations with scars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T08:10:03-07:00","id":1130269,"title":"","content":"That Monday Meeting post is great. I am so looking forward to this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:53:25-07:00","id":1130418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130180#post1130180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the revealed origins so far are accident, birth (in vivo?). My guess infection, surgury, fantastical for the rest. <br /> <br /> Clades Part Machine, Psionic, Animal Hybrid, guesses for the rest Mutation (the Hulk, jekle and Hyde) and Ritualist. <br /> <br /> Symbionant I think will be a variation for Animal Hybrid, not a clade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides In Vitro and Accident, I'm expecting Volunteer, Deception, Abduction, and Self-Inflicted as potential Origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:58:53-07:00","id":1130514,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if you're the architect of your own change, doesn't that make it easier to manage it? I mean, yes the change could have been purely accidental, but even then if you're familiar with the principles of your metamorphosis, shouldn't that give you some kind of advantage? In fact, how does the origin of your change affect you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:04:54-07:00","id":1130521,"title":"","content":"As soon as I got done reading the teaser, I had an idea for a super soldier program that involved splicing a human with ant DNA. Super strength, perfect coordination, that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> It... doesn't go over so well... for either the test subject, or the scientists who made him! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:31:21-07:00","id":1130540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130521#post1130521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as I got done reading the teaser, I had an idea for a super soldier program that involved splicing a human with ant DNA. Super strength, perfect coordination, that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> It... doesn't go over so well... for either the test subject, or the scientists who made him! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...sooooooo...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig01.deviantart.net/a864/f/2012/342/0/d/kamen_rider_ichigo_wallpaper_by_touchboyj_hero-d5ndwwn.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Ok fine: he's supposed to be a grasshopper and not an ant.<br /> <br /> Although...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fk5B-bCrY4U\" data-code=\"Fk5B-bCrY4U\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Fk5B-bCrY4U/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:32:28-07:00","id":1130542,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm a bit hesitant about the concept that Deviants lose their ability to define themselves by individuality.<br /> <br /> If this game is using the escaped experiment angle, then I think they would be even more inclined towards individuality, instead of depending on others to assure them of who they are.<br /> <br /> The concept of forced transhumanism has been around for decades, if not longer. But those stories almost always revolve around the escaped test subject trying to make their own choices.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You're not a weapon, you're a person. Don't let what they did to you define who you are!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This sounds like it's using a different approach, in which the Deviant has no choice but to let others define them. In which case, I have to wonder how / why they managed to escape their creators in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:35:44-07:00","id":1130543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130418#post1130418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides In Vitro and Accident, I'm expecting Volunteer, Deception, Abduction, and Self-Inflicted as potential Origins.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very possible, I'm curious as what Origins do mechanically, Clade at least is partly obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:39:53-07:00","id":1130547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130540#post1130540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...sooooooo...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not exactly. More like he's strong as hell, can burrow through the ground and has the ability to command legions of ants (via pheromones). As his mutations become progressively worse, he slowly mutates into a nightmarish hybrid of man and insect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:53:20-07:00","id":1130556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130542#post1130542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm a bit hesitant about the concept that Deviants lose their ability to define themselves by individuality.<br /> <br /> If this game is using the escaped experiment angle, then I think they would be even more inclined towards individuality, instead of depending on others to assure them of who they are.<br /> <br /> The concept of forced transhumanism has been around for decades, if not longer. But those stories almost always revolve around the escaped test subject trying to make their own choices.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You're not a weapon, you're a person. Don't let what they did to you define who you are!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This sounds like it's using a different approach, in which the Deviant has no choice but to let others define them. In which case, I have to wonder how / why they managed to escape their creators in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the thing keeping you (mostly) sane is your burning desire to get even with a particular person, how are you not letting that relationship define you?<br /> <br /> (Yes, this is fucked up. The Remade are fucked up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:05:38-07:00","id":1130563,"title":"","content":"A mad scientist obsessed with creating artificial super powers has been field testing his work using human - animal hybrids. His most recent and greatest success is his own 10 year old daughter, who he spliced with reptilian DNA, and has begun to manifest pyrokinetic abilities.<br /> <br /> They call her 'Lil, Dwagon.'<br /> <br /> <br /> (Idea came from my City of Villains days. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:34:04-07:00","id":1130611,"title":"","content":"Heh it occurs to me that there was a pack of these in Hunting Ground: Rockies. They were su'ur, victims of the Gurdilag who, with their creator gone, were left as free-willed abominations that could never be werewolf again. There was Broken Web, whose soul was merged with an azlu soul shard. Tastes of Sibling Flesh, whose soul is now shared with a spirit of cannibalism. And Dream of Lost Days, a werewolf known for her prophetic gifts whose soul was merged with a powerful regret spirit. There was also the Bastard Son, whose soul was merged with a unihar.<br /> <br /> I imagine ex-supernatural template borne characters aren't possibility in the core. But idigam like to play with mortals too. Seems like a really fun game, I'm super excited about it, especially the freedom available in origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:05:28-07:00","id":1130629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130611#post1130611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh it occurs to me that there was a pack of these in Hunting Ground: Rockies. They were su'ur, victims of the Gurdilag who, with their creator gone, were left as free-willed abominations that could never be werewolf again. There was Broken Web, whose soul was merged with an azlu soul shard. Tastes of Sibling Flesh, whose soul is now shared with a spirit of cannibalism. And Dream of Lost Days, a werewolf known for her prophetic gifts whose soul was merged with a powerful regret spirit. There was also the Bastard Son, whose soul was merged with a unihar.<br /> <br /> I imagine ex-supernatural template borne characters aren't possibility in the core. But idigam like to play with mortals too. Seems like a really fun game, I'm super excited about it, especially the freedom available in origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't one of the Idigam in the 2e core create similar horrors by mashing souls together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:21:11-07:00","id":1130631,"title":"","content":"Most of them do, it's a subset of their Essence Shaping powers, Forge Servant. There's even Divine Clay to change someone's physical assets. One of them has its own 'species,' the Mawspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:56:42-07:00","id":1130711,"title":"","content":"<b>Well that's just great. I think I'm addicted to this now... SO MANY POSSIBILITIES!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. A perverted geneticist in Japan really wanted to create his own cat girl. Maybe he should have tried using house cats, instead of tigers!<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. A wannabe witch dabbles in a grimoire she can barely translate and ends up casting the wrong spell. Now, her soul has merged with an ethereal being and the two struggle for control of her body.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. Puberty is never pretty, your body starts going through all these changes and it's really confusing at first. But nothing in your sex ed class mentioned anything about mutating into an entirely different species! Turns out, somebody in your recent ancestry was an alien shapeshifter, and you inherited their genes. Now, men in black suits are trying to capture you for research.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4. A crippled soldier offers himself for testing a new form of experimental prosthetics. Upon waking up from the surgery, he finds that his new implants include military grade hardware and is told his body is now property of the government! They're pretty sure that this is a violation of their basic human rights, however, so when the government assigns them to their first mission, they go AWOL.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5. Psionic abilities run strong in your family; they've been cultivating them for centuries. And now after countless generations of carefully selected breeding, they've produced you. One of the most talented psychics in the family's collective history. It wouldn't be so bad, if your family wasn't obsessed with power. They don't see you as their relative, they see you as an asset to be used and exploited. You couldn't stomach it anymore, so you ran away from home. That's when your parents put out a reward for your 'safe' return!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-18-2017, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:04:48-07:00","id":1130712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1130711#post1130711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon