=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:33:59-08:00","id":1159695,"title":"","content":"I think the extra time is wroth it to fit the powers theme","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T09:55:21-08:00","id":1160240,"title":"","content":"All that extra work just for one character is going to get it vetoed by most STs. Plus, it massively slows down scenes if whenever you use that power, the ST has to look at or make up the backstory for every single character present at the scene and choose or homebrew an appropriate Condition for every single one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T18:59:24-08:00","id":1161040,"title":"","content":"Good point hmmmm well i need to find a new from the power takes maybe it.makes people depprssed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:59:46-08:00","id":1163257,"title":"","content":"Info on Theme, Mood, Style, &amp; Tone: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T19:07:07-08:00","id":1163796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re metaphorically the chronically ill or differently-abled</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(in a comment about what Deviant 100% isn\u2019t) Accepting your changes</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m probably gonna get backlash from this, but these two things together rubbed me the exact wrong way and I hate it. I was really excited for Deviant before, but hounestly this killed any hype I had for it. I\u2019m terribl at explaining things, so I won\u2019t try to go into one of those great lectures from other people in this forum, but this feels like like 2 utterly unreconciable themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T20:14:21-08:00","id":1163803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163796#post1163796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m probably gonna get backlash from this, but these two things together rubbed me the exact wrong way and I hate it. I was really excited for Deviant before, but hounestly this killed any hype I had for it. I\u2019m terribl at explaining things, so I won\u2019t try to go into one of those great lectures from other people in this forum, but this feels like like 2 utterly unreconciable themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I kinda get where you\u2019re coming from, but consider that the \u201cillness\u201d and \u201cdisablement\u201d in question were purposefully afflicted by a third party who sees you as a commodity to be exploited. That\u2019s not so acceptable when on the receiving end of it, is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T20:47:07-08:00","id":1163808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163803#post1163803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I kinda get where you\u2019re coming from, but consider that the \u201cillness\u201d and \u201cdisablement\u201d in question were purposefully afflicted by a third party who sees you as a commodity to be exploited. That\u2019s not so acceptable when on the receiving end of it, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m tired and don\u2019t really have the eloquence to give a long winded answer, but<br /> 1. It has been pointed put that deviants can be accidents or caused by themselves or just completly independent of everybody <br /> 2. You could say the same thing about war inguries at a highly decreased level, and those people manage to accept their changes<br /> 3. If they are intentionally supposed to be metaphorically chronically ill or differently abled, tying them into a box of must be angry all the time and being perpetually self loathing hurts their represemtation, especially considering this is Onyx paths\u2019s first real forray at taking a look at those issues beyond small nods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:08:59-08:00","id":1163814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163803#post1163803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I kinda get where you\u2019re coming from, but consider that the \u201cillness\u201d and \u201cdisablement\u201d in question were purposefully afflicted by a third party who sees you as a commodity to be exploited. That\u2019s not so acceptable when on the receiving end of it, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> The &quot;toxic waste leak&quot; from the research facility that gave half the town cancer wasn't an accident. The &quot;careless scientists&quot; intentionally exposed you and your neighbors to a dangerous and unpredictable extradimensional toxin whose properties occasionally cause victims to manifest superhuman abilities. They intended to exploit the most useful of these through a third party intermediary pretending to oppose them. People died because of those scientists' ambition - friends, family, neighbors, and even some assholes (but no one deserves to go out like this). Your body is rotten with tumors, too, but you were one of the &quot;success stories.&quot; You even worked for them for awhile in exchange for experimental cancer treatments that at least helped keep you out of the hospital for a few months between relapses. Until you found out that the philanthropic organization was just another arm of the same research group that arranged the &quot;accident&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> What if your metamorphosis really was just the result of an accident? Well, the explosion took your sight - burned the eyes right out of your skull. So that sucks. But the fact that it left you with the ability to see and communicate with beings in a parallel universe has kept you from adapting to your disability and moving on with your life. Your life has become a never ending parade of strangers who want to understand your &quot;gift&quot; or hope you will use it to benefit them - some of whom have proven unwilling to take no for an answer.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you've got resentment at the very least and quite probably a towering rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:51:49-08:00","id":1163822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163814#post1163814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;toxic waste leak&amp;quot; from the research facility that gave half the town cancer wasn't an accident. The &amp;quot;careless scientists&amp;quot; intentionally exposed you and your neighbors to a dangerous and unpredictable extradimensional toxin whose properties occasionally cause victims to manifest superhuman abilities. They intended to exploit the most useful of these through a third party intermediary pretending to oppose them. People died because of those scientists' ambition - friends, family, neighbors, and even some assholes (but no one deserves to go out like this). Your body is rotten with tumors, too, but you were one of the &amp;quot;success stories.&amp;quot; You even worked for them for awhile in exchange for experimental cancer treatments that at least helped keep you out of the hospital for a few months between relapses. Until you found out that the philanthropic organization was just another arm of the same research group that arranged the &amp;quot;accident&amp;quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> What if your metamorphosis really was just the result of an accident? Well, the explosion took your sight - burned the eyes right out of your skull. So that sucks. But the fact that it left you with the ability to see and communicate with beings in a parallel universe has kept you from adapting to your disability and moving on with your life. Your life has become a never ending parade of strangers who want to understand your &amp;quot;gift&amp;quot; or hope you will use it to benefit them - some of whom have proven unwilling to take no for an answer.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you've got resentment at the very least and quite probably a towering rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>God <i>damn</i> I wanna play this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:59:38-08:00","id":1163824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163808#post1163808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m tired and don\u2019t really have the eloquence to give a long winded answer, but<br /> 1. It has been pointed put that deviants can be accidents or caused by themselves or just completly independent of everybody <br /> 2. You could say the same thing about war inguries at a highly decreased level, and those people manage to accept their changes<br /> 3. If they are intentionally supposed to be metaphorically chronically ill or differently abled, tying them into a box of must be angry all the time and being perpetually self loathing hurts their represemtation, especially considering this is Onyx paths\u2019s first real forray at taking a look at those issues beyond small nods.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ve managed to exclude the part where people are trying to exploit you for your condition, even if your condition was self-imposed. You\u2019ve also failed to highlight the difference between afflictions caused by human but faceless forces (e.g. war), and the ones with very clear faces (the Conspiracies). How can one just accept and move on, when there are people who\u2019d very much not like to for their own profit? Those are the points the where the anger and defiance stems from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T01:19:43-08:00","id":1163843,"title":"","content":"How many types of Deviant exist, regarding the creation process? By technological means (Adam Jensen), by magical means (Shadowman)...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:04:00-08:00","id":1163870,"title":"","content":"Biology psyich and psychological in my opinion <br /> Seriously no more pain treatment can be possible but dull you to other things as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:03:58-08:00","id":1163882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163824#post1163824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You\u2019ve managed to exclude the part where people are trying to exploit you for your condition, even if your condition was self-imposed. You\u2019ve also failed to highlight the difference between afflictions caused by human but faceless forces (e.g. war), and the ones with very clear faces (the Conspiracies). How can one just accept and move on, when there are people who\u2019d very much not like to for their own profit? Those are the points the where the anger and defiance stems from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I get that, but my point is more the metaphorical meaning of it is terrible, and to say they aren\u2019t that is to take away from what is directly said. If they are metaphorically this group, then they need to represent that, and saying that shouldn\u2019t matter because of the empirical rules takes away from what these people spend their lives trying to do, by saying that\u2019s the way you get fucked over. Imagine if in Changeling one of the themes was that it was better when you were under the True Fae\u2019s Control. That would take away from all the themes and metaphorical meaning and actual people Changeling is about at a certain level, even if the mechanics supported that and the game sounded cool and played well. I\u2019m not saying the game doesn\u2019t make sense if you take it at face value and within the game\u2019s context, I\u2019m saying these two ideas are utterly unreconciable. I like the ideas and the worldbuilding, but the subtext kills me and I can\u2019t not express that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:25:15-08:00","id":1163890,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... How would you feel about the following statement:<br /> &quot;When it comes to stages of grief, a Deviant campaign covers denial, bargaining, depression and most of all - anger. Attaining acceptance is sabotaged by Conspiracies that hound your step, and as such is both endgame material and a victory condition.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:42:12-08:00","id":1163896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163890#post1163890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... How would you feel about the following statement:<br /> &amp;quot;When it comes to stages of grief, a Deviant campaign covers denial, bargaining, depression and most of all - anger. Attaining acceptance is sabotaged by Conspiracies that hound your step, and as such is both endgame material and a victory condition.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I like that. That\u2019s hounestly a good theme and I enjoy what it is saying and represents a journey where there is an understanding that you can get acceptance. If this is what the game is about, completely hounestly I\u2019m quite exited. But the direct statement that Deviant isn\u2019t about accepting the change sort of directly went into a turn off for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:09:30-08:00","id":1163926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163896#post1163896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the direct statement that Deviant isn\u2019t about accepting the change sort of directly went into a turn off for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That direct statement is part of the same point as Deviant not being about characters who like being monsters or are quote-unquote Independent From Other People.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're not going to see the game written to support Remade Renegades who don't engage with humanity and are fine in doing so&quot; does not scan to &quot;The Remade are allegories for the chronically ill and the differently abled, who of course experience No Interpersonal Issues Whatsoever from missing something that most of society takes for granted, ergo this particular supernatural alteration in a setting filled with cost-intensive supernatural alterations shouldn't have a firm subtextual stance against Deviant characters diving headfirst into isolation from humanity in the long term without consequence.&quot;<br /> <br /> The phrase exists as part of an immediate context that fits just fine into the larger discussion \u2014 Deviants share Prometheans' issue of &quot;your powers aren't stable and they're going to fuck you up if the Conspiracies don't beat them to the punch,&quot; which makes the Renegade equivalent to the hypothetical Complacent Centimanus extra untenable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:55:21-08:00","id":1163944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163896#post1163896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I like that. That\u2019s hounestly a good theme and I enjoy what it is saying and represents a journey where there is an understanding that you can get acceptance. If this is what the game is about, completely hounestly I\u2019m quite exited. But the direct statement that Deviant isn\u2019t about accepting the change sort of directly went into a turn off for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that we carry different assumptions and because of that we've interpreted the same line of text completely differently.<br /> You read it as &quot;The game does not acknowledge the possibility of moving beyond your pain&quot;.<br /> I read it as &quot;The game is about what happens before closure, with the risk of never getting there, or losing it once you have it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not accepting the changes can also be understood differently.<br /> I assumed it meant &quot;The changes you're going through leave you worse off - you're a victim, not a superhero&quot;.<br /> You saw it as &quot;You will never grow as a person and make peace with your changes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The final product might still leave some room for interpretation, but odds are that as time passes on, we get to learn which of us had a closer guess. Either way, your heart is in the right place and I hope the book lives up to all our best expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:23:41-08:00","id":1163953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163926#post1163926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That direct statement is part of the same point as Deviant not being about characters who like being monsters or are quote-unquote Independent From Other People.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;You're not going to see the game written to support Remade Renegades who don't engage with humanity and are fine in doing so&amp;quot; does not scan to &amp;quot;The Remade are allegories for the chronically ill and the differently abled, who of course experience No Interpersonal Issues Whatsoever from missing something that most of society takes for granted, ergo this particular supernatural alteration in a setting filled with cost-intensive supernatural alterations shouldn't have a firm subtextual stance against Deviant characters diving headfirst into isolation from humanity in the long term without consequence.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The phrase exists as part of an immediate context that fits just fine into the larger discussion \u2014 Deviants share Prometheans' issue of &amp;quot;your powers aren't stable and they're going to fuck you up if the Conspiracies don't beat them to the punch,&amp;quot; which makes the Renegade equivalent to the hypothetical Complacent Centimanus extra untenable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hounest to god, I like those other points and if it wasn\u2019t for this one thing I would be super exited for just everything that Deviant is. The quote is notable to me because accepting that you are different isn\u2019t the same as reveling in it like you say. These people can still be connected and be a \u201cpart of humanity\u201d while still being ok with it being a thing that they are different now. It isn\u2019t \u201cI\u2019m not human and that\u2019s great!\u201d It\u2019s \u201cI\u2019m not the same as I was and I can deal with that.\u201d From What I\u2019ve seen (and what I assume because of some want to avoid huge overlap), Deviants are explicitly different from Prometheans in that Prometheans aren\u2019t human and can become that way, Deviants were human, aren\u2019t anymore, and they can\u2019t go back. There aren\u2019t Centimanus because they don\u2019t have the option to go back normally, only mitigate it. I agree with you that That none of those things are what I want, but acceptance isn\u2019t those things. It\u2019s gritting your teeth and saying that you can deal with it at a certain level. Houesntly, If The thing Teatime said the stages of grief and the acceptance game end are true, I\u2019m probably more excited for the game then I\u2019ve ever been before and really want to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:17:05-08:00","id":1163968,"title":"","content":"Deviant doesn't have an endgame of escaping your condition - your character's hurt will always be with him. You can, however, mitigate it somewhat, by finding other outlets for the pain. A Deviant who develops their lesser Integrity-equivalent to be greater than their main one enters a state where their Scars don't need anywhere near as much upkeep, and they can get a measure of peace by throwing themselves into what their new touchstones represent.<br /> <br /> But the hurt is still there, and the character remains Remade. If the primary trait goes above the secondary one again, the period of remission ends.<br /> <br /> For Renegades, balance requires developing Loyalty - the story archetype of the survivor finding something or someone else to live for. They will never lose their Scars, but they can put them to the back of their mind for a while, until something happens to disrupt that peace.<br /> <br /> It's not an &quot;end game&quot; in the sense that some of our other games have. It's possible for a freshly-created Deviant to achieve after only a few stories; but it's fragile, and most characters trying for it will drop in and out of it over the course of their Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Which, for my money (obviously) makes it fit the metaphor more - you can choose to not let the condition define you, but it won't magically disappear and you will <i>always</i> have it.<br /> <br /> That's as much Acceptance as a Deviant can have; exchanging a self-destructive coping mechanism for a more positive one. If they try to go without one entirely, they go Brindlefly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:54:08-08:00","id":1163983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1163968#post1163968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, for my money (obviously) makes it fit the metaphor more - you can choose to not let the condition define you, but it won't magically disappear and you will <i>always</i> have it.<br /> <br /> Th