oin Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:55:58-07:00","id":1224267,"title":"","content":"&quot;Deviant's [power stat] goes from 0 to 5. It's not that difficult, you just have to figure out something else to base Supernatural Tolerance on,&quot;-Dave","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 06-02-2018, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T17:18:02-07:00","id":1227918,"title":"","content":"I recently began watching the anime D Grayman. I think the exorcists make a good example of a bunch of loyalists, and the main character already has an impressive set of scars. The thing they call innocence appears to be an alien artifact/entity with it's own agenda. I am only up to episode 5 at this time. If I am right the main character will become increasingly less human as he is thrown into more and more battles until he becomes just another puppet of the innocence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T04:35:02-07:00","id":1228002,"title":"","content":"I was just reminded of this on another thread, but I think Phyrexia from Magic the Gathering could have some good inspiration for Deviant. They are biomechanical abominations who acquire mutations by way of con