e_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1228747#post1228747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Deviant who blows out my transforming into a prehistoric beast? Sounds pretty fun to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, Dino Squad, I had forgotten about that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T17:23:07-07:00","id":1230130,"title":"","content":"Street Sharks the old cartoon show, as well as TMNT works too (I know the main TMNT heroes weren't human to start, but the concept of mutated experiments hiding from conspiracies holds here too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T17:33:24-07:00","id":1230132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1230130#post1230130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Street Sharks the old cartoon show, as well as TMNT works too (I know the main TMNT heroes weren't human to start, but the concept of mutated experiments hiding from conspiracies holds here too)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm hoping that 'something turned into a mostly human' is an option in the game now. Most likely to show up in a supplement rather tgan the Core I admit, but playing the lost children of Dr. Moreau fits the concept of the game rather well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T18:11:15-07:00","id":1230141,"title":"","content":"If you can be turned into a cyborg an animal-person isn't that far fetched. Though changeling is probably the better game for it not being a hideous monstrosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T19:11:28-07:00","id":1230146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1230132#post1230132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I'm hoping that 'something turned into a mostly human' is an option in the game now. Most likely to show up in a supplement rather tgan the Core I admit, but playing the lost children of Dr. Moreau fits the concept of the game rather well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave mentioned that human-animal hybrids (called Chimerics) were among the x-splats in the core book, and I imagine that could be easily re-flavored to be what you want. I figure the Chimerics will be this gameline's Beast Changelings/Gangrel/Prey equivalent. One of the aspects of Deviant I anticipate is its adaptability and open-endedness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 06-25-2018, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T08:53:56-07:00","id":1230555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1230132#post1230132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm hoping that 'something turned into a mostly human' is an option in the game now. Most likely to show up in a supplement rather tgan the Core I admit, but playing the lost children of Dr. Moreau fits the concept of the game rather well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean something that started out as a nonhuman, I don't think that's likely. But I'd be very surprised if human with animal stuff grafted on won't be an option, and it's unlikely you wouldn't be able to use the rules to model the other way round.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T11:01:55-07:00","id":1230596,"title":"","content":"On the contrary; there have been hints that \u201csomething that started out as non-human\u201d is very much doable in <b>Deviant</b>. It's not the main focus of the game; but it's not out of the question either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-30-2018, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T14:49:35-07:00","id":1230648,"title":"","content":"I do want to play a character that just recently got Sapient,,!! See <a href=\"https://www.vertigocomics.com/graphic-novels/we3\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.vertigocomics.com/graphic-novels/we3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:47:38-07:00","id":1230662,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Konradleijon;n1230648]I do want to play a character that just recently got Sapient,! /QUOTE]<br /> I imagine such a thing will be mechanically possible(there were Changelings that lost sapience over their Durance, not to mention Prometheans), but that sounds rather daunting to roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 06-30-2018, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:57:08-07:00","id":1230665,"title":"","content":"I figured they'd be more available as NPCs like retainers or familiars. We've brought up We3 before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T09:16:45-07:00","id":1230832,"title":"","content":"Earlier in this thread we where discussioning reedfeld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T05:43:07-07:00","id":1231080,"title":"","content":"Regardless of source, exploring the idea of continuity of consciousness extending prior to self-awareness could make for some interesting character arcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T12:34:17-07:00","id":1231181,"title":"","content":"What how do we know dogs aren\u2019t already aware elephants are sapient","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T12:44:48-07:00","id":1231182,"title":"","content":"Dogs are actually found out to be self aware","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:08:47-07:00","id":1231226,"title":"","content":"See .how do we know other humans are sapient (I think there for I am)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:44:26-07:00","id":1231236,"title":"","content":"Let's not have the animal intellence debate here. It is at best a tangent off discussion of a hypothetical alteration of a potential splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T06:57:35-07:00","id":1232849,"title":"","content":"The scenario has everything to have a fully focused Aliens add-on. Humans kidnapped and modified by beings who can not actually enter this world for some unintelligent purpose and who do not want to help in that purpose who may be working for it unconsciously, while the aliens use the few resources that can enter into contact with this world to redirect the rebel deviants for their purposes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T15:17:09-07:00","id":1232941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1232849#post1232849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scenario has everything to have a fully focused Aliens add-on. Humans kidnapped and modified by beings who can not actually enter this world for some unintelligent purpose and who do not want to help in that purpose who may be working for it unconsciously, while the aliens use the few resources that can enter into contact with this world to redirect the rebel deviants for their purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that also sounds like Changeling to me. Splitting hairs on the concept though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T17:16:03-07:00","id":1232959,"title":"","content":"Er, why not both?<br /> <br /> Still not sure what folks don't like about aliens, especially in a post-<i>Realms of Atlantis </i>world. <br /> <br /> I'm patient though. Looking forward to Changeling next month, devouring the Geist backer updates currently, and waiting for a Hunter and/or Deviant kickstarter in the future. Plenty of time to get to other supernatural gribblies in the far future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T02:34:48-07:00","id":1233020,"title":"","content":"I do like aliens; just noting that we already had something that fits that role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T04:33:38-07:00","id":1233032,"title":"","content":"Changeling I think lacks the Body Horror that a lot of kidnapped-by-aliens fiction has. In Changeling, the horror is the trauma of the kidnapping itself, the helplessness of being there as they operate on you. In Deviant, the horror is being back on earth, and feeling your heart beat on the wrong side of your chest, and feeling something move under your chest, and screaming &quot;what have they done to me!&quot; Changeling also uses the Durance as a sort of opening-to-a-world-of-fancy, where sure you were kidnapped by aliens, but your best friend was a candle that burned as Shahrazade told her 1001 stories, and your boyfriend was a billy-goat crossing a troll-bridge. You may have been kidnapped by aliens, but once you enter the Changeling society, it becomes clear that you're all being forced to play sick cosplay-as-torture by the fickle gods of Faerie. <br /> To me, that weakens the usefulness of Changeling to tell certain types of alien-abduction stories. It doesn't make much sense to me for the abduction victims to return with the kind of Contracts that Changelings get. Deviant now, Deviant's body-horror themes fit better here, at least in my opinion. <br /> <br /> But I know that this is a long and hashed-over argument on these forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T05:50:11-07:00","id":1233037,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t worry about which gameline represents extraterrestrials \u201cthe best,\u201d overlapping niches or not. I mean, before Mummy we had mummies (Purified, Osirans, certain vampires), and before Demon we had demons (Inferno, and too many to count), but those games proved we could have more. And I never thought I needed Beast until I got it. Deviant seems like it\u2019ll do just fine if people want to run alien abduction stories, with or without Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T07:00:10-07:00","id":1233043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1233032#post1233032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling I think lacks the Body Horror that a lot of kidnapped-by-aliens fiction has.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps the body horror is not physically present (to normal mortals), but it is still very much there.<br /> <br /> Have you ever heard of body dysmorphic disorder? It's a psychological condition in which a person rejects pieces of their own body because they are under the delusion that they are somehow foreign or aggressive. In the most extreme cases, victims have attempted to amputate or surgically modify their bodies just to ease their condition.<br /> <br /> Now, you take somebody like a Changeling, who can see through the mask and realize they're physiology isn't what it's supposed to be and starts freaking out over it. From a mortal's point of view, they're going to see an ordinary human screaming about how their own body is some sort of abomination, or has even turned against them.<br /> <br /> That can lead to some extremely disturbing stories if handled correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T07:14:22-07:00","id":1233047,"title":"","content":"Not the tangent i wanted to go with. Sorry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:40:47-07:00","id":1233274,"title":"","content":"On a different tangent off alienation, Amalgam seems interesting. From what we've heard, it seems like they consist of two consciousnesses imperfectly fused together. Will they be &quot;synergistic&quot; like Geists, monsters within you you must hold back and appease like Horrors, or perhaps a split personality that takes over periodically? Or something completely different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 07-08-2018, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:45:28-07:00","id":1233277,"title":"","content":"In that case, the Fatal Frame twins are Amalgam?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:50:14-07:00","id":1233278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1233277#post1233277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, the Fatal Frame twins are Amalgam?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think so, likewise Lucy/Nyu from Elfin Lied (though I imagine she will be one of those characters that can fit multiple splats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T00:46:16-07:00","id":1233360,"title":"","content":"Anyone notice Stitch is a deviant, lilo is a touchstone and the enemy agency is dr. Hamsterville?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T13:50:00-07:00","id":1233495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div 