strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1236712#post1236712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be a good idea to make a thread to collect people's various Deviant concepts? Obviously as more info about the game comes out and eventually publication occurs, ideas can get refined to use the appropriate terms and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they won't drown out more definite news of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:38:28-07:00","id":1236880,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Will it be possible to combine powers of scientific origin with magical origin?<br /> <br /> More than that, it will be possible to have other splat capabilities. Like a cyborg having some psychic power.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <hr /></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:05:04-07:00","id":1236891,"title":"","content":"CoD loves its magitech, so probably. Given how they described Forms, you could probably add a little cyborg to your psychic-based character or vice-versa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:43:51-07:00","id":1236903,"title":"","content":"Hell, you could probably have a symbiote (that is a splat I believe) be a person with a lovecraftian horror in him, or a cyborg with an ever expanding sentient AI","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:28:36-07:00","id":1237242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1236880#post1236880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will it be possible to combine powers of scientific origin with magical origin?<br /> <br /> More than that, it will be possible to have other splat capabilities. Like a cyborg having some psychic power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clade is the trait that governs the look and form of a Deviant's variations and scars - so I think cyborg is one of the Clades, But they're also written to be independent of the Deviant's origin - an example being that a cyborg might have been created through the catastrophic failure of a magical rite to summon a machine spirit. So yes to the first.<br /> <br /> The second, I doubt they'll be much if any attention paid to them having powers beyond those in the Deviant core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:09:54-07:00","id":1237259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1237242#post1237242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second, I doubt they'll be much if any attention paid to them having powers beyond those in the Deviant core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that there will be powers within each Clade and universal powers (Simbionte seems to be such a case of power).<br /> <br /> But I'm really worried if it will be possible to buy exclusive powers from other clades. At first I hope it is but that this has a cost in terms of scars far greater than buying a power from your Clade or Universal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:38:42-07:00","id":1241474,"title":"","content":"So the broucher mentions that deviant is going to be on Kickstarter. Which I figured it would but it\u2019s still nice to see confirmation. Monday meeting notes announced the next Kickstarter already and it\u2019s not deviant. <br /> <br /> Think we are going to get the ks this year or next? None of the other chronicles of darkness books had a reference to being kickstarted. So they may be much later. <br /> <br /> But is there much else that looks like it be slated for Kickstarter? I didn\u2019t think deviant was that far down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:53:23-07:00","id":1241505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1241474#post1241474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the broucher mentions that deviant is going to be on Kickstarter. Which I figured it would but it\u2019s still nice to see confirmation. Monday meeting notes announced the next Kickstarter already and it\u2019s not deviant.<br /> <br /> Think we are going to get the ks this year or next? None of the other chronicles of darkness books had a reference to being kickstarted. So they may be much later.<br /> <br /> But is there much else that looks like it be slated for Kickstarter? I didn\u2019t think deviant was that far down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>This year is possible but I would say unlikely - the game is still in redlines.<br /> <br /> These days, it's pretty common for OPP to launch new game lines through a Kickstarter, so I don't think anyone is surprised by Deviant. It doesn't mean it's imminent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T13:21:22-07:00","id":1243007,"title":"","content":"Hell, it's amazing how open the &quot;experiment gone horrible wrong&quot; trope is. (Or even gone horribly right)<br /> <br /> How about a merrick institute tries forcing a horror into a kid, and instead of having it replacing his soul, is merged to it, seeping into the cracks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:10:49-07:00","id":1243172,"title":"","content":"I'd be somewhat wary of Beast/Deviant crossovers, given how open-ended Beast is, and how open-ended Deviant looks to be. As much as possible, I'd like to keep them distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:43:12-07:00","id":1243177,"title":"","content":"I'm just giving an idea for the merrick institute making a deviant, don't really see anything wrong with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:12:19-07:00","id":1243186,"title":"","content":"That's fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T16:38:30-07:00","id":1243326,"title":"","content":"People are way too overzealous about cautioning against crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T17:28:37-07:00","id":1243339,"title":"","content":"Yup, even when the game is not actually meant as a crossover, but that deviants can come from many different anomalies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T10:03:49-07:00","id":1257792,"title":"","content":"Souls are different in CofD from how they are depicted in a lot of settings. They are not necessarily associated with the psyche or self, they are interchangeable; if you lose yours, you lose your ability to self-actualize, but if you obtain another, even if it's not the one you were born with, you will still be &quot;you&quot;.<br /> <br /> What, then, do you suppose would happen if a normal human swapped souls with a Remade? We know that the Remade have damaged souls; would gaining a whole soul &quot;fix&quot; the Remade, or at least stop its degeneration? Would the human with the damaged soul begin to exhibit the physical peculiarities of the Remade it came from? Or would they perhaps lose their ability to define themselves, and end up with Loyalty and Conviction scores? Perhaps, in the process of cracking a Remade's soul, it becomes inextricably linked to its body and mind, and they cannot be disassociated. I seem to remember reading that Remade are very difficult to mind control as a result of their changes.<br /> <br /> I think this is pretty interesting to think about. Do any of you have opinions on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T11:09:41-07:00","id":1257803,"title":"","content":"I think it would be the loss of self identity. The remade have been altered so much their souls broke, this is what causes loss of identity, not mutations. I believe the misconception is that the broken soul is what causes mutations, it merely makes it harder to stabilize them.<br /> <br /> Think about the chieron corporation hunters, they have parts grafted to them, yet they are stable in general. This is due to the fact they have identity of self allowing stability. If they had a broken soul these parts could get worse, or they would merely gain derangments along loss of identity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T07:28:38-07:00","id":1257961,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Deviants lost their sense of self, so much as it was damaged by their transformations. They still have souls, they are still self-aware, but they tend to define their identity by how others see them, rather than how they see themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T03:50:00-07:00","id":1258171,"title":"","content":"Err, not quite. They tend to define their identity in terms of how they relate to others, which isn't quite the same as \u201chow others see them\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-13T10:41:24-07:00","id":1260439,"title":"","content":"How organizations make Renegades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUoltzjzMwE\" data-code=\"FUoltzjzMwE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FUoltzjzMwE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-13T11:36:32-07:00","id":1260442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1258171#post1258171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err, not quite. They tend to define their identity in terms of how they relate to others, which isn't quite the same as \u201chow others see them\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's pretty much the opposite - other people only matter to Remade in so much as whether the Remade sort them in the &quot;friends&quot; or &quot;enemies&quot; column.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T11:10:38-07:00","id":1260702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1260442#post1260442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's pretty much the opposite - other people only matter to Remade in so much as whether the Remade sort them in the &quot;friends&quot; or &quot;enemies&quot; column.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for completely new people they meet (that they don't ignore) they basically go &quot;Either help me or get the hell out of the way&quot;? If a person doesn't help them, do Deviants often/always consider them a hostile?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23709-cannox","name":"Cannox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23709_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T19:40:48-07:00","id":1260802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cannox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1260702#post1260702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for completely new people they meet (that they don't ignore) they basically go &quot;Either help me or get the hell out of the way&quot;? If a person doesn't help them, do Deviants often/always consider them a hostile?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't so much &quot;help me, or get out of my way&quot; as &quot;if you're nice to me, I will devote my life to protecting you and furthering your interests, but if you get in my way, I will make you curse the day you were born.&quot; Anyone who does neither is pretty close to beneath the Deviant's notice. That's not a choice for the Remade. That's the consequence of living with a shattered soul.<br /> <br /> I regard the Phantom of the Opera as a pretty good example of how some Deviants interact with a Loyalty Touchstone. Normally pretty reclusive, but on rare occasions, he reaches out to another human being. If you reciprocate, he'll do anything for you, rearrange his whole life and his corner of the world in an effort to make you happy and keep you safe. But that love is incredibly needy, jealous, always terrified that it will be betrayed, that he will lose you. If ever you betray him, his wrath will be terrible. He moves you from the &quot;friends&quot; column to the &quot;enemies&quot; column in his world, and then he redirects all the energy he spent trying to please you into effecting your utter ruin.<br /> <br /> Not all Deviants are quite so, um, clingy and stalker-ish. But this is definitely one of my favorite examples of the difference between &quot;healthy loyalty to one's friends and family&quot; and &quot;Loyalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> For Conviction, one of my favorites is the protagonist in Memento. Having gotten his revenge against his wife's murderer but being unable to savor that victory (because he can't remember it), he intentionally tricks himself into exacting his revenge a second time against someone who was directly involved in helping him get revenge the first time. You get the sense that this cycle will never, ever end. His thirst for revenge cannot be quenched, and he will always find someone else to blame and to brutally murder.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that having your physical, mental, and spiritual health utterly dependent on feeding your time and emotional energy into either protecting people or destroying them, that's probably not a recipe for maintaining healthy, long-term relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T20:17:09-07:00","id":1260810,"title":"","content":"It seems to fit the fiction.<br /> <br /> It's not like you get an in depth analysis on the relationship between the protagonist and background character #3 they never interacted with, I guess outside of Star Wars. In things like Incredible Hulk it's the waitress who's nice to him, and the trucker who thinks he looks weird and wants to bully him. Of course, blowing up in front of that extra character can always help the protagonist sort them out, or at least get them out of there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2018, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T20:42:20-07:00","id":1260817,"title":"","content":"Do the different clades have different ways of showing conviction and loyalty? How would a deviant who knew exactly what he was getting into, but not the full extent of consequences, react with conviction and loyalty knowing it's his fault","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T07:15:16-07:00","id":1260902,"title":"","content":"so there Yanderes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https