yxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T19:06:48-07:00","id":1261459,"title":"","content":"We don't know. All we know is that their souls just flat out broke.<br /> <br /> If you want, you could make a deviant missing his Ka","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T05:29:54-07:00","id":1261536,"title":"","content":"I don't think any parts are missing per se. Its all there but its just broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:19:01-07:00","id":1261586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1261432#post1261432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I wonder how their broken souls interact with Urging Ephemerals.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ew, bloody hell, I'm not touching <i>that</i>.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:25:54-07:00","id":1261589,"title":"","content":"So it\u2019s like how some animals won\u2019t go near they know is sick","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:55:19-07:00","id":1261595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1261586#post1261586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Ew, bloody hell, I'm not touching <i>that</i>.&amp;quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but what about spirits of decay, instability, rot, disease, insanity, etc<br /> <br /> Also, is it that they don't want to do it or that they can't? If the former, what happens if they Fetter themselves to a Deviant out of a desperate need to hide -right now- ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T10:00:48-07:00","id":1261600,"title":"","content":"Decay and similar spirits would work, but really, for a soul to just be broken must scary for a spirit.<br /> <br /> It should be noted deviants are so filled with hate, things such as mind control have a hard time affecting them, so perhaps possessing a deviant would have the spirit thinking &quot;oh shit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T11:51:42-07:00","id":1261628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1261536#post1261536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any parts are missing per se. Its all there but its just broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, they lack a sense of self-identity, of internal independence. They define themselves in relation to other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T18:13:18-07:00","id":1261680,"title":"","content":"I'm actually kinda confused by that. At the same time as I'm seeing it said that they have no internal self-image, I'm also seeing Dave Brookshaw say that they only relate to other people on a very basic level of friends, enemies and &quot;not important&quot;. I don't understand how those interact to create a creature that is close enough to human in thought to be a playable template. Frankly, I'm not sure how that first part even works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm hoping their &quot;friends, enemies, background scenery&quot; mental paradigm is not as immutable as I'm reading. I wouldn't want to play more than a couple sessions of a game where every character has to have a total extreme &quot;screw you, got mine&quot; attitude. I mean, how can you make a doctor who still wants to help people but is on the run from an unscrupulous pharmaceutical company that wants to turn his experiments to long-term profitable palliative therapies? Does the trauma make him lose his higher motivations? Can you put something as wide as &quot;sick people&quot; in the friends category?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-19-2018, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T18:30:15-07:00","id":1261683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1261680#post1261680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't want to play more than a couple sessions of a game where every character has to have a total extreme &quot;screw you, got mine&quot; attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reading a bit more into 'friends' and 'enemies' than I think was implied. It doesn't imply a mercenary mindset, it implies a survivor's mindset. Someone who has pressure on them and can't go around being free with trust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, how can you make a doctor who still wants to help people but is on the run from an unscrupulous pharmaceutical company that wants to turn his experiments to long-term profitable palliative therapies? Does the trauma make him lose his higher motivations? Can you put something as wide as &quot;sick people&quot; in the friends category? </div> </div> </div>This is something that's shown up in media. I'm pretty sure it, again, has been in the Incredible Hulk (among many, many other places), where David Banner was a doctor, and even though not a medical doctor, had similar training. Someone is injured (often a child) or about to give birth, and the Deviant wants to go, they need to go, but they do feel an urge to help. So they do, and it's a setback, the baddies chasing him catch up, their chance to get out of there is missed. But in the end, the person they helped in turn helps them, helping them get away or distracting the baddies, and everyone learns something.<br /> <br /> Even people who aren't doctors. Angie Spica, in the Wild Storm, for instance developed nanomachines to help people in emergency situations and in general, but is being hindered by the organization that, basically, just wants her to make devices to control humanity. She tests it on herself, wildly against the rules, and when she sees a man being thrown from a 20+ story building she can't help but activate them and go save him, even if it means she's going to lose her job, be hunted by her former employers, and likely be vivisected if she's ever caught.<br /> <br /> But of course you do have people who are entirely willing to let others die in front of them because they find it too bothersome to deal with them or they don't like blood or whatever. Not everyone's made out to do that. I don't think any game so far has restricted actions on that front. Vampires can be generous, werewolves can be pacifistic, mages can be ignorant, prometheans can choose not to try to be better, hunters can try to give up the vigil, changelings can return to arcadia, sin-eaters can disagree with their geist, beasts can choose not to be scary all the time, demons can go loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2018, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T18:41:42-07:00","id":1261686,"title":"","content":"It is a very common trope in fugitive stories, which is why I was worried that this mindset where it sounds to me like most people who haven't had any personal interaction with you are background scenery would make characters like that hard to play. <br /> <br /> Yeah, a normal human fugitive with an intact Integrity track might do that because of their Virtue, I worry that, as someone who tries to play characters the way the mechanics seem to be driving their story, won't have any willpower-based incentive to help out strangers unless a friend asks them too.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling for words here, but what I'm trying to get at is that the way the mechanics and the fluff (that we know of) sounds to me, Deviants just don't have the internal drive to help out strangers<br /> <br /> I probably am over thinking it, so could you explain some more where you think my misconceptions are coming from, it would be much appreciated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T18:54:00-07:00","id":1261689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1261686#post1261686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably am over thinking it, so could you explain some more where you think my misconceptions are coming from, it would be much appreciated</div> </div> </div> </div>I did expand on it (i'm big on editing my posts and I looked through a comic I'm reading at the moment to find an example), but really I'm a bigger proponent of waiting for the book. I love getting spoilers, but I think the book will go into it more than a post would.<br /> <br /> That said, without knowing anything about the mechanics, a doctor character might have an aspiration to help someone in need. And presumably there will be a reward for doing something that helps you, but hinders your ability to get away from whoever's coming after you. I think something like that has been confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T19:40:00-07:00","id":1261692,"title":"","content":"I parsed the &quot;friends and enemies&quot; comment through the lens of Borderline Personality Disorder, personally. Though obviously it's touchy comparing a real-life disorder to a fantasy monster, BPD is defined as &quot;...marked by an ongoing pattern of varying moods, <b>self-image</b>, and behavior&quot; and &quot;a pattern of intense and unstable relationships ... often swinging from <b>extreme closeness</b> and love (idealization) to e<b>xtreme dislike or anger</b> (devaluation).&quot; (<a href=\"https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/topics/borderline-personality-disorder/index.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a>)<br /> <br /> So when a Deviant likes you, they really LIKE you, and may develop very strong feelings about you very quickly (even if it's mostly projecting their own stuff onto you, like the need to be A Good Person or because you remind them of someone they lost). But they're also always on high alert for any possible sign of danger, no matter how slight or ambiguous, and pre-emptively lash out or withdraw from anyone who pings their danger sense, even (maybe especially) if it's the same person they were obsessed with two days ago.<br /> <br /> Not so much &quot;Anyone I don't feel strongly about is just scenery&quot; as &quot;I feel strongly about anyone that's not mere scenery.&quot; But we'll see if the corebook bears this version out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T19:40:59-07:00","id":1261693,"title":"","content":"In terms of identity, think the punisher. Sure he has his own personality and way of doing things, but ultimately, unbridled, pure hate drives his living. Similarly he has a hard time trusting people, just like a renegade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T21:25:40-07:00","id":1261711,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry Nofather. Didn't catch the edit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T06:59:08-07:00","id":1263784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bonus-origins-deviant-the-renegades/#comment-466517\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bonus-origins-deviant-the-renegades/#comment-466517\" target=\"_blank\"> Halloween Bonus! Origins [Deviant: The Renegades] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bonus-origins-deviant-the-renegades/#comment-466517\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bonus-origins-deviant-the-renegades/#comment-466517 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T07:42:54-07:00","id":1263793,"title":"","content":"Now that is some great news to hear. Origins actually seem pretty dang useful now that they are explained, and the volunteers can make for some tragic AND utterly selfish monsters.<br /> <br /> As for overt and covert, I'm geussing overt shows yours obvious deformities and can increase scars easier, while covert is weaker but hides yourself better and makes it harder to get a scar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T07:56:49-07:00","id":1263799,"title":"","content":"Yeah but I'm having trouble figuring out why mentality determines that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T08:32:51-07:00","id":1263804,"title":"","content":"Can you elaborate, it's simply what they tend to exhibit, like the autoterges or whatever they are called experiment themselves to hell, so they have obvious powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T09:32:59-07:00","id":1263811,"title":"","content":"Now here's a new question arising from the preview. What is Magnitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:02:38-07:00","id":1263821,"title":"","content":"I completely forgot to mention that. It definitely sounds like a big power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:06:45-07:00","id":1263822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1263799#post1263799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but I'm having trouble figuring out why mentality determines that</div> </div> </div> </div>The Conspiracies explicitly do not know. So I think the answer is &quot;come up with it yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> My guess is that it's due to the fact a Deviant's soul cracking is the source of their powers; different mindset, different way it cracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:31:35-07:00","id":1263827,"title":"","content":"It's rare for me to get political in i the internet,but I'm so curious. Is this game an anti-capitalist game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:33:54-07:00","id":1263828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1263827#post1263827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rare for me to get political in i the internet,but I'm so curious. Is this game an anti-capitalist game?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's against powerful people abusing less powerful people. Something that happened not only in capitalism,but in socialism and anarchism as well. So nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:37:46-07:00","id":1263831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1263827#post1263827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rare for me to get political in i the internet,but I'm so curious. Is this game an anti-capitalist game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is explicitly. Although the game seems to borrow plenty from the cyberpunk genre, and plenty of corporations in the Chronicles of Darkness would be up to some really shady business, a Conspiracy could just as easily be a covert research branch of the French government or a heretical shadow-sect of the Catholic Church. The game appears more to be about power, specifically the ways in which a powerful group can screw up a powerless individual, but also how the tables can be turned against the mighty through (maybe?) righteous anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:51:56-07:00","id":1263839,"title":"","content":"Don't think of the game as a political statement. It's just that one of the themes is that corruption of power leads to people being seen as objects to be used for their own benefits. Or even worse, makes people see themselves as inferior as humans, thus making them want to transcend it<br /> <br /> Also, anyone else notice the volunteer section having a conspiracy very familiar to the Chieron Group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T11:56:28-07:00","id":1263843,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T12:13:21-07:00","id":1263849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1263811#post1263811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here's a new question arising from the preview. What is Magnitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Context suggests that its the currency of power normally granted by scars, though of note it shares a name with the power stat of the rather autourgic alchemists from promethean.<br /> <br /> Not sure about &quot;subtle&quot; though. If its a game term it should be capitalized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T12:18:44-07:00","id":1263850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1263849#post1263849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Context suggests that its the currency of power normally granted by scars, though of note it shares a name with the power stat of the rather autourgic alchemists from promethean.<br /> <br /> Not sure about &quot;subtle&quot; though. If its a game term it should be capitalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it means that a &quot;average&quot; Magnitude is not subtle at all,but this one is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T14:10:38-07:00","id":1264495,"title":"","content":"Great, now I'm envisioning a human / reptilian hybrid as one of the Born.<br /> <br /> The shapeshifters came to earth to see if they could cross breed with our people!<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I want to say that the human side's pathological desire to express their individuality is what leads to them breaking, and thus rebelling against their creators. But individualism seems to oppose the idea that the remade depend on their attachments to others to prevent themselves from degenerating into monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-03-2018, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:58:24-07:00","id":1264510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1264495#post1264495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, now I'm envisioning a human / reptilian hybrid as one of the Born.<br /> <br /> The shapeshifters came to earth to see if they could cross breed with our people!<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I want to say that the human side's pathological desire to express their individuality is what leads to them breaking, and thus rebelling against their creators. But individualism seems to oppose the idea that the remade depend on their attachments to others to prevent themselves from degenerating into monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Individuality is what I hope will be explored in this game. As of now, I'm wondering how a remade's personality works or if they truly are bound by how they perceive other people whole heartedly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T17:01:43-07:00","id":1264529,"title":"","content":"i always thought it'd be really cool to mix Scion and Cofd. stories with gods who are also very dark. And i think Deviant may help with that. i'm visualiing a group of worshippers of a panteon who wnt to get close to their god,and so they capture an innocent bystander and through secret rites and forbidden magics,they turn the person into a incarnation of thor or vishnu or maybe artemis. the Deviant has a divine spirit inside him giving him Variations similar to a god's powers in the myths,their endgame meltdown would becoming so powerful you don't think like a person anymore,you are a god body and soul","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T17:29:28-07:00","id":1264531,"title":"","content":"Honestly that sounds realistic for the game as it sounds of now.<br /> <br /> Personally I can't believe we've never thought of the &quot;experiment gone horribly wrong (or right)&quot; monster trope before. It seems so obvious now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T23:28:05-07:00","id":1264565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1264529#post1264529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i always thought it'd be really cool to mix Scion and Cofd. stories with gods who are also very dark. And i think Deviant may help with that. i'm visualiing a group of worshippers of a panteon who wnt to get close to their god,and so they capture an innocent bystander and through secret rites and forbidden magics,they turn the person into a incarnation of thor or vishnu or maybe artemis. the Deviant has a divine spirit inside him giving him Variations similar to a god's powers in the myths,their endgame meltdown would becoming so powerful you don't think like a person anymore,you are a god body and soul</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you want to try applying that to the sci-fi genre, I would suggest using <b>Portal</b> and <b>System Shock</b> as inspiration material. Ultimately culminating in a <b>I Have No Mouth and I Must Scream</b> type of situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T10:32:54-08:00","id":1264753,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Modifications generated by contact with the Inhuman as Tyrants (Resident Evil) and Hastalyk Creatures (Call of Cthulhu) would be examples of Pathological? Could Deep-Human Hybrids be classified into Genotypal (the crosses were conducted by a cult and in ritual ceremonies prepared)?</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T10:21:59-08:00","id":1281323,"title":"","content":"Huh, now I'm trying to imagine a way to implement some sort of technological hivemind that assimilates organic creatures by forcefully turning them into cyborgs.<br /> <br /> One of the Deviants manages to interrupt the transformation process before it can assimilate their mind, kind of like Matthew Kane from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJwyjWpP4XA\" target=\"_blank\">Quake!</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:25:11-08:00","id":1282432,"title":"","content":"Have we heard anything about the children of Remade? Deviants are people who can no longer define themselves and require other people for a self-definition, so I think I would think some of them would try to have a family. I assume that it would require decisions to be made on a case-by-case basis, but it would be strange if there wasn't any guidance on the issue in the book. I'm sure that in a lot of cases they would not be affected by the changes to the Remade, and there will be many Remade that won't be able to have children at all. But what about those who can have children and have been changed genetically or supernaturally in such a way that it could pass on to their children like a curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:29:34-08:00","id":1282467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=1282432#post1282432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we heard anything about the children of Remade? Deviants are people who can no longer define themselves and require other people for a self-definition, so I think I would think some of them would try to have a family. I assume that it would require decisions to be made on a case-by-case basis, but it would be strange if there wasn't any guidance on the issue in the book. I'm sure that in a lot of cases they would not be affected by the changes to the Remade, and there will be many Remade that won't be able to have children at all. But what about those who can have children and have been changed genetically or supernaturally in such a way that it could pass on to their children like a curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that many children of Remade may become Remade of the Genotypal Origin, inheriting some of their parent's altered nature, but manifesting in unique ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":